1
00:00:01,201 --> 00:00:04,605
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:04,605 --> 00:00:07,474
♪ SOMEWHERE IN TIME
AND SPACE ♪

3
00:00:07,474 --> 00:00:10,711
♪ MIKE NELSON
AND HIS ROBOT PALS ♪

4
00:00:10,711 --> 00:00:13,747
♪ ARE CAUGHT IN
AN ENDLESS CHASE ♪

5
00:00:13,747 --> 00:00:16,783
♪ PURSUED BY A WOMAN
WHOSE NAME IS PEARL ♪

6
00:00:16,783 --> 00:00:19,987
♪ AN EVIL GAL WHO WANTS
TO RULE THE WORLD ♪

7
00:00:19,987 --> 00:00:22,890
♪ SHE THREW A FEW THINGS
IN HER PURSE ♪

8
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:24,558
♪ AND IN HER ROCKET SHIP
SHE HUNTS HIM ♪

9
00:00:24,558 --> 00:00:26,560
♪ ALL ACROSS THE UNIVERSE ♪

10
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:29,363
[PEARL]
I’LL GET YOU!

11
00:00:29,363 --> 00:00:32,232
♪ I’LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

12
00:00:32,232 --> 00:00:35,769
♪ THE WORST I CAN FIND--
LA LA LA ♪

13
00:00:35,769 --> 00:00:38,639
♪ HE’LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

14
00:00:38,639 --> 00:00:41,775
♪ AND I’LL MONITOR HIS MIND--
LA LA LA ♪

15
00:00:41,775 --> 00:00:44,645
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND,
MIKE CAN’T CONTROL ♪

16
00:00:44,645 --> 00:00:48,148
♪ WHERE THE MOVIES BEGIN
OR END-- LA LA LA ♪

17
00:00:48,148 --> 00:00:51,084
♪ HE’LL TRY TO KEEP
HIS SANITY ♪

18
00:00:51,084 --> 00:00:53,553
♪ WITH THE HELP
OF HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

19
00:00:56,156 --> 00:00:57,524
♪ ROBOT ROLL CALL ♪

20
00:00:57,524 --> 00:00:59,226
YOU’RE ON!

21
00:00:59,226 --> 00:01:00,427
OH, MY STARS!

22
00:01:00,427 --> 00:01:02,095
CHECK ME OUT!

23
00:01:02,095 --> 00:01:03,563
I’M DIFFERENT!

24
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:04,998
♪ IF YOU’RE WONDERING HOW ♪

25
00:01:04,998 --> 00:01:06,700
♪ HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

26
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:09,870
♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS--
LA LA LA ♪

27
00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:12,673
♪ JUST REPEAT TO YOURSELF,
"IT’S JUST A SHOW ♪

28
00:01:12,673 --> 00:01:15,976
♪ I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX" ♪

29
00:01:15,976 --> 00:01:19,046
♪ FOR MYSTERY
 SCIENCE THEATER ♪

30
00:01:19,046 --> 00:01:22,549
♪ 3000 ♪

31
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:38,498
MM, HI EVERYONE.
CROW, SERVO, GLAD YOU’RE HERE.

32
00:01:38,498 --> 00:01:40,701
JUST GOT THIS, UH,
NOTICE FROM GYPSY.

33
00:01:40,701 --> 00:01:44,371
- APPARENTLY SHE’S GOTTA WORK ON
THE MAIN SWITCHING UNIT.
- HUH.

34
00:01:44,371 --> 00:01:46,473
I DON’T KNOW.
SO IN A COUPLE OF MINUTES,
THE POWER’S GOING TO GO DOWN.

35
00:01:46,473 --> 00:01:47,741
- YES!
- WOOHOO!

36
00:01:47,741 --> 00:01:49,509
HEY, HEY, HEY! I KNOW
WHAT YOU’RE THINKING,

37
00:01:49,509 --> 00:01:51,278
AND NO LOOTING THIS TIME.
YOU UNDERSTAND?

38
00:01:51,278 --> 00:01:52,379
[SWITCH CLICKS]

39
00:01:52,379 --> 00:01:53,847
- WOW!
- WOOHOO!

40
00:01:53,847 --> 00:01:57,117
[GLASS SHATTERING]

41
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:59,386
[CLATTERING]

42
00:02:03,724 --> 00:02:05,993
[SWITCH CLICKS]

43
00:02:05,993 --> 00:02:07,561
ALL RIGHT,
WHAT DID YOU LOOT?

44
00:02:07,561 --> 00:02:09,096
WELL, I BROKE INTO
MY OWN ROOM,

45
00:02:09,096 --> 00:02:11,164
AND MANAGED TO GET AWAY
WITH MY TV.

46
00:02:11,164 --> 00:02:13,800
[CHUCKLES]
I’LL NEVER MISS IT.

47
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,235
OKAY. TOM?

48
00:02:15,235 --> 00:02:17,671
AH, WELL, I THREW A MANNEQUIN
THROUGH YOUR WINDOW, MIKE--

49
00:02:17,671 --> 00:02:19,639
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.
WHERE’D YOU GET A MANNEQUIN?

50
00:02:19,639 --> 00:02:21,675
WELL, I KEEP ONE
FOR POWER OUTAGES.

51
00:02:21,675 --> 00:02:22,976
ANYWAY, THREW IT
THROUGH YOUR WINDOW,

52
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:25,312
MANAGED TO GET AWAY
WITH YOUR RECYCLING HERE.

53
00:02:25,312 --> 00:02:27,547
I’M NOT A VERY GOOD
LOOTER, AM I?

54
00:02:27,547 --> 00:02:28,815
- NO, NO YOU’RE NOT.
- NO.

55
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,050
WE’LL BE RIGHT BACK.

56
00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:32,753
IF IT GOES OUT AGAIN,
I’M GRABBING MY BLENDER.

57
00:02:36,223 --> 00:02:40,827
♪♪

58
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:44,197
[GLASS SHATTERING]

59
00:02:44,197 --> 00:02:45,465
ALL RIGHT,
WHAT DID YOU LOOT NOW?

60
00:02:45,465 --> 00:02:47,501
LOOT? NO, NO LOOTING.

61
00:02:47,501 --> 00:02:49,870
I JUST ACCIDENTALLY
DROPPED AN ANVIL INTO YOUR BOX

62
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:51,271
OF COMMEMORATIVE PLATES

63
00:02:51,271 --> 00:02:53,273
OH, HEY LOOK.
PEARL’S CALLING.

64
00:02:53,273 --> 00:02:55,976
WANNA GET THAT?

65
00:02:55,976 --> 00:03:00,614
AND THEN
I WILL RULE THE WORLD!

66
00:03:02,249 --> 00:03:04,518
[LAUGHS]

67
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:07,287
THAT NEEDS A LITTLE BACKGROUND,
DOESN’T IT?

68
00:03:07,287 --> 00:03:10,190
THE DEAL IS, SMELLSON,
I’M GOING TO RULE THE WORLD.

69
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,792
BUT YOU DON’T RULE THE WORLD

70
00:03:11,792 --> 00:03:13,927
BY GOING AT IT
ALL SCATTERSHOT.

71
00:03:13,927 --> 00:03:17,898
NOPE, SLOW AND STEADY
WINS THE RACE, OLD NUT.

72
00:03:17,898 --> 00:03:20,300
SO, I’M GOING TO RULE
THE WORLD,

73
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:21,802
BUT I’M GOING TO DO IT

74
00:03:21,802 --> 00:03:25,539
ONE PERSON AT A TIME.

75
00:03:25,539 --> 00:03:28,341
[LAUGHS]

76
00:03:28,341 --> 00:03:29,676
NOW, WHO’S FIRST?

77
00:03:29,676 --> 00:03:31,178
HERE...

78
00:03:31,178 --> 00:03:33,246
A MR. TODD GUNDERSON, MA’AM.

79
00:03:33,246 --> 00:03:35,482
AH, GUNDERSON EH?

80
00:03:35,482 --> 00:03:36,783
UH, TODD’S FINE.

81
00:03:36,783 --> 00:03:38,885
TODD. TODD, GOOD.

82
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:41,021
WELL, TODD...

83
00:03:41,021 --> 00:03:43,857
WHAT DO YOU SAY? CAN I RULE YOU?
CAN I? HUH? CAN I?

84
00:03:43,857 --> 00:03:46,093
RULE ME? UH, NO.

85
00:03:46,093 --> 00:03:47,494
PLEASE?

86
00:03:47,494 --> 00:03:51,331
NO!

87
00:03:51,331 --> 00:03:53,934
WHAT IF I SAID I’D KILL YOU
IF YOU DIDN’T LET ME?

88
00:03:53,934 --> 00:03:57,304
UH, I’M SORRY, I REALLY
DON’T FEEL THAT THREATENED.

89
00:03:57,304 --> 00:03:59,106
GET OUT OF HERE.

90
00:03:59,106 --> 00:04:01,374
NEXT.

91
00:04:01,374 --> 00:04:03,777
A MR. TOM SERVO, MA’AM.

92
00:04:03,777 --> 00:04:05,378
HEY, GUYS! HERE I AM!

93
00:04:05,378 --> 00:04:07,114
HEY, GLAD TO HELP.

94
00:04:09,416 --> 00:04:10,684
[TOGETHER]
SERVO?

95
00:04:10,684 --> 00:04:13,353
YUP, IT’S ME.
BRAIN-GUY BROUGHT ME DOWN.

96
00:04:13,353 --> 00:04:16,256
MY NAME WAS NEXT ON THE LIST.
TOTALLY RANDOM! IT’S WEIRD.

97
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:19,860
SO, TOM SERVO,
WHAT DO YOU SAY? CAN--

98
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:20,927
WHAT? WHAT? WHAT?

99
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:22,863
DON’T I KNOW YOU
FROM SOMEWHERE?

100
00:04:22,863 --> 00:04:24,898
IT COULD BE.
I DO GET AROUND.

101
00:04:24,898 --> 00:04:28,301
THE TOM JONES THEATER
IN BRANSON, MISSOURI.

102
00:04:28,301 --> 00:04:31,004
YOU TRIED TO STEAL MY PURSE,
AND I BEAT YOU WITHIN--

103
00:04:31,004 --> 00:04:33,607
NO, NO, NO. MUST HAVE BEEN
SOME OTHER LUCKY GUY.

104
00:04:33,607 --> 00:04:36,042
WELL, IT’S NOT IMPORTANT.

105
00:04:36,042 --> 00:04:37,477
CAN I RULE YOU?

106
00:04:37,477 --> 00:04:40,380
SORRY, BABY.
NOBODY RULES THE TOM MONSTER.

107
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:43,416
DAMN, YOUR DEFENSES
ARE IMPENETRABLE.

108
00:04:43,416 --> 00:04:46,219
BRAIN-GUY, SEND MIKE THE MOVIE
WHILE I FIGURE OUT

109
00:04:46,219 --> 00:04:47,921
THIS WHOLE
WORLD RULING THING.

110
00:04:47,921 --> 00:04:50,790
CERTAINLY. MIKE,
YOUR MOVIE TODAY IS,

111
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:53,026
IF ONE CAN MEASURE
THESE THINGS,

112
00:04:53,026 --> 00:04:55,929
THE WORSE THING TO EVER
COME OUT OF CANADA.

113
00:04:55,929 --> 00:04:58,165
- WHOA.
- IT’S CALLED
 THE FINAL SACRIFICE.

114
00:04:58,165 --> 00:05:00,734
 [WOBBLY DIGITAL SOUND]

115
00:05:00,734 --> 00:05:02,169
UH, MA’AM, MAY I HAVE THE ROBOT?

116
00:05:02,169 --> 00:05:04,137
- OH, YES, OF COURSE.
- THEY NEED HIM FOR THE MOVIE.

117
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,872
SO LONG, TOOTS.
TAKE ME UP, CURLY.

118
00:05:05,872 --> 00:05:08,608
CURLY? WHY, I NEVER...

119
00:05:12,078 --> 00:05:14,014
[PANTING]

120
00:05:17,117 --> 00:05:19,619
HERE I AM, GUYS! GUYS?

121
00:05:19,619 --> 00:05:20,754
[MIKE]
WE’RE IN THE THEATRE.

122
00:05:20,754 --> 00:05:23,423
- [GRUNTS]
- COME ON, DUMMY!

123
00:05:35,969 --> 00:05:37,671
OH, ME, I DON’T GIVE
A FLYING DUTCHMAN

124
00:05:37,671 --> 00:05:38,872
ABOUT THIS PRODUCTION.

125
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:46,746
HUH, I UNDERSTAND EVERYTHING
UP TO THE WORD "A."

126
00:05:46,746 --> 00:05:49,649
HE COMES FROM
A LONG LINE OF GREIDANUSES.

127
00:05:51,585 --> 00:05:54,821
[MOUTH ECHOES]

128
00:05:57,424 --> 00:06:00,660
HOORAY! THE MOVIE’S CLOSED TODAY
BECAUSE OF SNOW!

129
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:02,762
[CROW CAWING]

130
00:06:02,762 --> 00:06:06,166
THINK MAYBE THIS IS
A DOCUMENTARY ABOUT MAPLE SYRUP?

131
00:06:09,436 --> 00:06:13,340
YOU BROUGHT THE FACEMASK,
YOU NUT.

132
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:16,009
HE’S CHECKING
HIS BIORé STRIP.

133
00:06:20,847 --> 00:06:24,684
[HUMMING, BEATBOXING]

134
00:06:24,684 --> 00:06:28,255
I THINK THE MOVIE’S
GOING REALLY WELL.

135
00:06:28,255 --> 00:06:30,090
YEAH.

136
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:31,291
DON’T WORRY ABOUT ME, BOSS.

137
00:06:31,291 --> 00:06:33,960
THE HAIR ON MY BACK
IS KEEPING ME WARM.

138
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:35,662
YEAH.

139
00:06:39,499 --> 00:06:42,902
BETH PLUS JASON.

140
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:45,105
RAY DAVIES?

141
00:06:50,610 --> 00:06:54,581
UGH, AH MAN, I DON’T KNOW.
I SLEPT WEIRD. UGH.

142
00:07:02,055 --> 00:07:04,791
BIGFOOT FOR
WRANGLER RELAXED FIT.

143
00:07:08,695 --> 00:07:12,299
RANDY BACHMAN IS BEING PURSUED
BY SADOMASOCHISTS.

144
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,972
[GULPING]

145
00:07:18,972 --> 00:07:22,375
NO FAIR, YOU GUYS,
I LOST MY MOON BOOTS.

146
00:07:26,346 --> 00:07:29,983
MY FACE IS WARM,
BUT MY SHOULDERS ARE FREEZING.

147
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:39,659
NOBODY LEAVES
THE WORLD WRESTLING FEDERATION.

148
00:07:41,594 --> 00:07:44,731
COME BACK HERE,
SYRUP RUSTLER!

149
00:07:48,501 --> 00:07:51,204
THAT’S HIS WINTER TANK-TOP.

150
00:07:55,041 --> 00:07:57,277
CANADIAN RULES FOOTBALL
IS MUCH DIFFERENT.

151
00:07:57,277 --> 00:08:00,547
YEAH, MAN.

152
00:08:00,547 --> 00:08:03,783
I DON’T KNOW, I’M JUST HAPPY.

153
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:10,657
AH, I FORGOT A MOUTH HOLE.

154
00:08:10,657 --> 00:08:14,027
BEETHOVEN’S FIFTH JUST
CAN’T GET STARTED, HERE.

155
00:08:18,231 --> 00:08:20,533
HI, CINDY.

156
00:08:24,938 --> 00:08:26,139
[GUNSHOT]

157
00:08:26,139 --> 00:08:28,274
OH, HE EXPLODED BEFORE
THEY COULD SHOOT HIM.

158
00:08:28,274 --> 00:08:29,409
OH.

159
00:08:32,278 --> 00:08:34,614
HE CHANGED HIS NAME FROM
I BELIEVE IN SOMETHING,

160
00:08:34,614 --> 00:08:37,083
BUT I DON’T REALLY
GO TO CHURCH MALCOLM.

161
00:08:39,619 --> 00:08:44,023
OH, GREAT,
THE SCORE IS SKIPPING.

162
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:46,493
OH, COME ON! ONE MORE SACRIFICE
BEFORE WE GO!

163
00:08:46,493 --> 00:08:48,795
OKAY, BUT THIS IS
THE FINAL SACRIFICE!

164
00:08:48,795 --> 00:08:50,463
GOODIE, GOODIE.

165
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:57,404
GO AWAY, SHANE. GO AWAY!

166
00:08:57,404 --> 00:08:59,372
HEY, RON ANDERSON HERE,
JUST GOTTA NIP DOWN

167
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:03,009
AND MAKE THAT MOVIE
REAL GOOD THEN.

168
00:09:03,009 --> 00:09:05,612
THAT’S AN ILLEGAL USE
OF A SILENT CONSONANT.

169
00:09:08,314 --> 00:09:10,984
YOU KNOW WHAT, THIS HAS THE
BACONEY STINK OF CANADA

170
00:09:10,984 --> 00:09:13,119
- ALL OVER IT.
- ALREADY.

171
00:09:14,921 --> 00:09:17,991
[HUMMING]

172
00:09:17,991 --> 00:09:21,661
I AM ZOMBOR. KELLY ZOMBOR.

173
00:09:28,301 --> 00:09:31,137
I HOPE HIS WOODEN SHOES
GET ICED UP AND HE CRASHES.

174
00:09:31,137 --> 00:09:32,772
YEAH.

175
00:09:32,772 --> 00:09:36,242
THAT’S AN ANAGRAM FOR
"DIRECT TO VIDEO."

176
00:09:39,079 --> 00:09:40,780
SEVEN YEARS
AFTER THE CREDITS?

177
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:43,316
I-- I GUESS.

178
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:47,954
WELL.

179
00:09:47,954 --> 00:09:49,556
YOU KNOW WHAT, PEOPLE
ARE JUST DYING TO--

180
00:09:49,556 --> 00:09:51,758
NO!

181
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:53,560
SORRY.

182
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:55,361
WELL, I BETTER GET BACK
TO MY GRAVE.

183
00:09:55,361 --> 00:09:58,264
SUN’S BEEN UP AN HOUR,
I’M STARTING TO DISINTEGRATE.

184
00:10:02,402 --> 00:10:03,837
HE WAS A GOOD HAMSTER.

185
00:10:03,837 --> 00:10:05,738
HELLO, DAD.

186
00:10:05,738 --> 00:10:08,041
IT’S BEEN A LONG TIME.

187
00:10:08,041 --> 00:10:10,310
I MISS YOU.

188
00:10:10,310 --> 00:10:12,011
I WANT TO KNOW
WHAT HAPPENED TO YOU.

189
00:10:12,011 --> 00:10:15,482
I DIED.

190
00:10:15,482 --> 00:10:17,517
WHAT?

191
00:10:17,517 --> 00:10:21,621
OH, A MAUSOLEUM WITH
A FINISHED EXPANSION UPSTAIRS.

192
00:10:25,859 --> 00:10:27,327
OH, THIS IS WHERE
THEY GET ALL THE STUFF

193
00:10:27,327 --> 00:10:29,796
TO PUT IN T.G.I. FRIDAYS.

194
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:35,735
HOW MANY GEEKS DOES IT TAKE
TO SCREW IN A LIGHT BULB?

195
00:10:35,735 --> 00:10:37,070
HOW MANY?

196
00:10:37,070 --> 00:10:40,740
I DON’T KNOW.
THAT WHY I’M ASKING YOU?

197
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:43,343
[SIGHS]

198
00:10:43,343 --> 00:10:46,980
MAN, HE IS JUST POURED
INTO THAT SWEATER.

199
00:10:50,083 --> 00:10:52,485
THIS SCENE WAS LIT
BY AN ITTY-BITTY BOOK LIGHT.

200
00:10:56,789 --> 00:10:58,424
THIS IS WHERE
I’VE SECRETED AWAY

201
00:10:58,424 --> 00:11:00,159
ALL MY RED SWEATERS.

202
00:11:02,028 --> 00:11:03,530
OH, BOY.

203
00:11:03,530 --> 00:11:06,432
HE’S GOING TO FIND OUT
HIS DAD IS A RODEO CLOWN.

204
00:11:11,538 --> 00:11:14,607
I DON’T CARE IF I’M TOO OLD,
I’M GETTING MY BATMAN PAJAMAS

205
00:11:14,607 --> 00:11:16,042
BACK OUT OF HERE.

206
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:22,615
HE WAS MADE IN THE IMAGE
OF AN EGG NOODLE.

207
00:11:24,484 --> 00:11:27,020
WELL, IF I’M GOING TO BE
A VENTRILOQUIST DUMMY,

208
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:29,789
I BETTER LEARN HOW TO LIVE
IN THIS TRUNK.

209
00:11:35,295 --> 00:11:37,263
[GRUNTS]

210
00:11:39,332 --> 00:11:42,802
NOW I’M GOING TO SETTLE IN
WITH THE BOOK OF MORMON.

211
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:50,543
LARRY CSONKA!

212
00:11:57,517 --> 00:12:00,353
[SNIFFS]
OOH, SHOULDN’T HAVE FILED
THAT SANDWICH.

213
00:12:02,922 --> 00:12:06,593
I’VE GOT TO FIND THE WARRANTEE
ON THIS SWEATER.

214
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:17,136
♪ AND I WILL BE THE ONE
TO HOLD LARRY CSONKA DOWN ♪

215
00:12:17,136 --> 00:12:18,771
♪ KISS HIM SO HARD ♪

216
00:12:18,771 --> 00:12:21,474
♪ I’LL TAKE LARRY CSONKA’S
BREATH AWAY ♪

217
00:12:24,110 --> 00:12:27,080
SOME GUYS CAN REALLY
PULL OFF LEGGINGS.

218
00:12:29,115 --> 00:12:32,218
I CAN’T WAIT UNTIL THEY START
THE INTERNET.

219
00:12:32,218 --> 00:12:35,488
HE’S WORKING ON
HIS BUD CORT SCRAPBOOK.

220
00:12:39,459 --> 00:12:41,427
AH, I’M GLAD I DON’T HAVE
ANY FRIENDS,

221
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:43,730
BECAUSE THEN I WOULDN’T BE ABLE
TO DO THIS.

222
00:12:46,899 --> 00:12:50,670
MAN, I’M 25,
I HOPE I HIT PUBERTY SOON.

223
00:12:53,272 --> 00:12:56,509
I KNOW, I’LL CALL
PRETENDING I’M BOB GRIESE.

224
00:12:58,945 --> 00:13:02,048
AH, FINALLY. GRANDMA’S HEAD.

225
00:13:10,189 --> 00:13:13,860
NO WONDER DAD LOST HIS MONEY,
HE INVESTED IN LEMON MINES.

226
00:13:16,929 --> 00:13:21,300
SEE CHEERLEADERS, CLASSMATES,
TEACHERS I DON’T LIKE...

227
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:25,505
A-HA, HERE IT IS.
THE TRANSCRIPTS FROM

228
00:13:25,505 --> 00:13:28,474
THE SPASSKY-KASPAROV MATCH
OF ’82.

229
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:31,544
OKAY. DEVIL, LIVING ROOM,

230
00:13:31,544 --> 00:13:33,579
DEN, FAMILY ROOM,

231
00:13:33,579 --> 00:13:37,150
ANOTHER DEVIL.

232
00:13:37,150 --> 00:13:39,118
TO MIKE PIPPER.

233
00:13:39,118 --> 00:13:40,920
OH, HE’S A PIPPER.
WOULDN’T YOU LIKE TO BE A--

234
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:42,422
NO, NO!

235
00:13:42,422 --> 00:13:44,490
MAN.

236
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:45,591
DON’T.

237
00:13:45,591 --> 00:13:47,360
[GRUNTS]

238
00:13:50,763 --> 00:13:54,300
AH, SEX, MALE. SEE, I AM.

239
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:56,469
IT SAYS, "DO NOT WRINKLE."

240
00:13:56,469 --> 00:13:59,105
"DEAR MIKE, I HAD
A CLOSE CALL TODAY.

241
00:13:59,105 --> 00:14:00,473
"THE CULT IS ON MY HEELS.

242
00:14:00,473 --> 00:14:02,642
"THE MAP IS NO LONGER
SAFE WITH ME.

243
00:14:02,642 --> 00:14:06,279
"IT IS THE ONLY COPY LEFT.
THE OTHERS I HAVE DESTROYED.

244
00:14:06,279 --> 00:14:08,081
"WE’LL MEET AGAIN SOON.

245
00:14:08,081 --> 00:14:11,317
BE CAREFUL.
YOUR PARTNER, THOMAS."

246
00:14:11,317 --> 00:14:14,954
YES, THERE’S WEIGHT-GAIN POWDER
IN THE FRIDGE.

247
00:14:20,093 --> 00:14:22,628
SO IT’S NEAR
A PONDEROSA STEAKHOUSE.

248
00:14:25,164 --> 00:14:27,533
I’M GONNA COLOR IT.

249
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:30,203
♪♪

250
00:14:35,808 --> 00:14:37,744
[HUMMING]

251
00:14:41,347 --> 00:14:44,951
MORNING, LARRY.

252
00:14:44,951 --> 00:14:47,587
THE TIME IS 6:4.

253
00:14:49,789 --> 00:14:52,525
DELAYED PUBERTY AWARENESS
PROGRAMS, HERE.

254
00:14:57,864 --> 00:15:01,601
MAN, THERE’S AN AMAZING NUMBER
OF CSONKAS.

255
00:15:06,172 --> 00:15:09,475
[GRUNTS]

256
00:15:09,475 --> 00:15:10,676
SO WE’RE JUST
WATCHING SOMEONE

257
00:15:10,676 --> 00:15:12,245
FRITTER AWAY
THEIR AFTERNOON HERE.

258
00:15:12,245 --> 00:15:14,147
MM-HM.

259
00:15:14,147 --> 00:15:16,849
- OPERATOR.
 - HI, COULD I HAVE
INFORMATION, PLEASE?

260
00:15:16,849 --> 00:15:18,518
 ONE MOMENT, PLEASE.

261
00:15:18,518 --> 00:15:22,288
NOW, THAT’S TWO MOMENTS.
I’M SORRY.

262
00:15:22,288 --> 00:15:23,656
 INFORMATION.

263
00:15:23,656 --> 00:15:25,525
HI, COULD I HAVE THE NUMBER
FOR MIKE PIPPER?

264
00:15:25,525 --> 00:15:26,592
NO.

265
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:28,895
P-I-P-P-E-R.

266
00:15:28,895 --> 00:15:30,830
 FOR WHAT CITY, PLEASE?

267
00:15:30,830 --> 00:15:34,200
- FROM EAGLEHAT.
 - ONE MOMENT.

268
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:37,170
EAGLEHAT?

269
00:15:37,170 --> 00:15:39,605
 I’ SORRY, THERE’S NO LISTING
 FOR AN M. PIPPER.

270
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:41,007
OH, OKAY, THANKS.

271
00:15:41,007 --> 00:15:45,511
AND THE INVESTIGATION
COMES TO A CLOSE.

272
00:15:45,511 --> 00:15:48,781
WELL, I BETTER GET TO READING
MY X-MEN COMICS.

273
00:15:52,518 --> 00:15:57,023
HEY, GET THIS CATERPILLAR
OFF MY LIP.

274
00:15:57,023 --> 00:15:59,759
WELL, LARRY,
I GUESS I BETTER GET GOING.

275
00:15:59,759 --> 00:16:03,262
SAY HELLO
TO JIM KIICK FOR ME.

276
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:06,933
[DOOR KNOCKS]

277
00:16:06,933 --> 00:16:10,203
COME IN.

278
00:16:10,203 --> 00:16:13,472
MRS. COSTANZA!

279
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:15,708
THERE. WHAT ARE YOU STUDYING?

280
00:16:15,708 --> 00:16:17,143
FRENCH REVOLUTION.

281
00:16:17,143 --> 00:16:19,779
OH, THAT LOOKS MORE LIKE
WORLD WAR II.

282
00:16:19,779 --> 00:16:21,614
[CHUCKLES]
OH, I’M A CAUTION.

283
00:16:21,614 --> 00:16:23,816
WHERE DID YOU GET THAT?

284
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:25,351
I FOUND IT IN THE ATTIC.

285
00:16:25,351 --> 00:16:28,287
LEAVE ME ALONE, MOM.
I’M STARTING A SOFTWARE COMPANY.

286
00:16:28,287 --> 00:16:29,856
WELL, DON’T WORK TOO LATE.

287
00:16:29,856 --> 00:16:31,724
I’LL LOCK YOU IN AS USUAL.

288
00:16:31,724 --> 00:16:34,026
WHAT WAS HE LIKE?

289
00:16:34,026 --> 00:16:37,063
NOW, TROY, WE’VE TALKED
ABOUT THIS BEFORE.

290
00:16:37,063 --> 00:16:39,165
I DON’T WANT YOU TO CRY
ABOUT WHAT IS PASSED.

291
00:16:39,165 --> 00:16:42,001
NO EMOTIONS.
WE’VE DISCUSSED THAT.

292
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:43,870
IS THAT WHY YOU LOCKED UP
HIS STUFF IN THE ATTIC?

293
00:16:43,870 --> 00:16:45,771
YOU DIDN’T WANT ME
TO GET UPSET?

294
00:16:45,771 --> 00:16:48,040
YOU FOUND THAT--?

295
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:51,177
TROY, YOU HAD
NO BUSINESS THERE.

296
00:16:51,177 --> 00:16:54,480
MY FATHER IS MY BUSINESS.

297
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:57,917
AL LOUIS AS GRANDMA.

298
00:16:57,917 --> 00:17:01,354
OH, TROY, I’M SORRY.

299
00:17:01,354 --> 00:17:03,789
I ONLY WANT YOU
TO FORGET HIM.

300
00:17:03,789 --> 00:17:05,358
CARRY ON WITH YOUR OWN LIFE.

301
00:17:05,358 --> 00:17:07,326
YEAH, ONCE YOU GET ONE.

302
00:17:12,465 --> 00:17:13,766
AM I LIKE HIM?

303
00:17:13,766 --> 00:17:17,303
NO, HE WAS MASCULINE
AND LIKABLE.

304
00:17:17,303 --> 00:17:19,171
YES.

305
00:17:19,171 --> 00:17:20,840
YOU’RE VERY MUCH LIKE HIM.

306
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:23,509
IF I’M THINKING
OF THE RIGHT GUY.

307
00:17:26,178 --> 00:17:29,949
MAN, NOW MY ROOM STINKS
OF YOUTH DEW.

308
00:17:32,351 --> 00:17:37,156
MVP, SUPER BOWL VIII
FOR MIAMI.

309
00:17:37,156 --> 00:17:39,258
SEVEN YEARS LATER.

310
00:17:40,459 --> 00:17:42,962
[CAR ENGINE FAILING]

311
00:17:42,962 --> 00:17:45,464
THAT’S ENOUGH TREES
FOR THE SPOTTED OWL, ISN’T IT?

312
00:17:45,464 --> 00:17:46,933
SURE.

313
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:52,371
UH-OH, THE TOWN’S ALTERNATOR
IS SHOT.

314
00:17:56,509 --> 00:17:59,645
FREE PICTURES OF BRIAN MULRONEY
WITH FILL UP.

315
00:18:04,383 --> 00:18:07,453
OH, AND WHO SAYS THERE AREN’T
ANY NICE HOMES IN CANADA?

316
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:18,531
CHECK IT OUT.

317
00:18:18,531 --> 00:18:22,902
SOMEONE’S SCRATCHING
HIS BELLY.

318
00:18:22,902 --> 00:18:24,770
DAMN!

319
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:28,407
WHEN IT’S ABOVE 50 OR BELOW 40
IT NEVER STARTS.

320
00:18:33,813 --> 00:18:37,249
CANADA IS FOR LOVERS.

321
00:18:39,852 --> 00:18:40,886
HIS TRUCK WON’T START,

322
00:18:40,886 --> 00:18:43,489
BUT AT LEAST
HIS TABLECLOTH IS DRY.

323
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:50,629
IF YOU LIVED HERE,
YOU’D BE IN HELL BY NOW.

324
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:54,467
CHECK OUT
THE LINC HAYES TOPIARY.

325
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:57,837
COOL.

326
00:18:57,837 --> 00:18:59,939
[HUMMING]

327
00:18:59,939 --> 00:19:02,641
HITCHCOCK’S PARADE OF HOMES.

328
00:19:06,278 --> 00:19:10,616
AW, IT’S
THE CAME-WITH-THE-FRAME FAMILY.

329
00:19:10,616 --> 00:19:12,551
WATER ME!

330
00:19:12,551 --> 00:19:17,089
[COUGHING]

331
00:19:17,089 --> 00:19:20,292
HEY, ANOTHER KID
EXACTLY LIKE HIM ACROSS TOWN.

332
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:24,430
HE JUST FINISHED
HIS EXHAUSTIVE

333
00:19:24,430 --> 00:19:27,133
FOUR-VOLUME BIOGRAPHY
OF LARRY CSONKA.

334
00:19:27,133 --> 00:19:30,002
[CLOCK CHIMES]

335
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:33,906
SOMEONE’S HITTING A FRY PAN,
WHICH MEANS IT’S 8:00.

336
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:38,611
OF COURSE THE CLOCK’S SET
TO MIAMI TIME.

337
00:19:42,281 --> 00:19:45,818
WELL, SWING CHOIR AIN’T GONNA
REHEARSE ITSELF.

338
00:19:49,955 --> 00:19:51,657
CALLED IN
FOR THE NIGHT SHIFT.

339
00:19:51,657 --> 00:19:55,194
APPARENTLY AUNTIE NEVER
GOT LAID-OFF AFTER THE WAR.

340
00:20:01,067 --> 00:20:03,736
WHY DID HE PUT A LASERDISC
IN THE REFRIGERATOR.

341
00:20:05,971 --> 00:20:07,606
HEY, EL SANTO!

342
00:20:07,606 --> 00:20:08,874
HEY!

343
00:20:12,411 --> 00:20:16,048
AH, LET’S SEE IF THERE’S ANY
LARRY CSONKA MOVIES ON TONIGHT.

344
00:20:22,021 --> 00:20:23,956
CAN I DISCIPLINE YOU?

345
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:29,795
[CHEWING SOUNDS]

346
00:20:29,795 --> 00:20:33,299
COLD CRAZY BREAD. MM.
REALLY IS CRAZY.

347
00:20:36,135 --> 00:20:40,239
WAIT, I HAVEN’T READ TOLKIEN
IN ALMOST A WEEK.

348
00:20:42,208 --> 00:20:46,178
SCRIPT IS PUNCHED UP
BY HARPO MARX.

349
00:20:46,178 --> 00:20:49,348
AH, A YANNI SONG
IS ABOUT TO BEGIN.

350
00:20:54,954 --> 00:20:58,057
WHAT WOULD
COACH DON SHULA DO?

351
00:21:05,097 --> 00:21:06,599
[GRUNTING SOUNDS]

352
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:09,768
IT’S HIS MICHAEL FEINSTEIN
SIGNATURE BAT.

353
00:21:12,972 --> 00:21:16,775
TEE-HEE, TEE-HEE.

354
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:20,679
HIS HEAD IS STILL
FACTORY WRAPPED.

355
00:21:20,679 --> 00:21:23,916
IS HE A DOOR-TO-DOOR
EXECUTIONER?

356
00:21:37,763 --> 00:21:40,666
OW! I WAS JUST GOING TO
READ THE METER.

357
00:21:46,071 --> 00:21:47,940
YOU KNOW IT’S SPRING
WHEN THE EXECUTIONERS

358
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:49,842
START GETTING IN THE HOUSE.

359
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:57,216
IT’S OPEN. PLEASE.

360
00:22:02,388 --> 00:22:04,957
THE McCULLOCHS ARE HERE.

361
00:22:13,132 --> 00:22:16,202
CAN I INTEREST YOU
IN A REPLACEMENT DOOR?

362
00:22:22,074 --> 00:22:26,478
CANADIAN VILLAIN,
GARTH VADER.

363
00:22:26,478 --> 00:22:29,281
ICKY FLAKES. UGH.

364
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:33,586
AH, THAT WAS
A GOOD SEVEN YEARS.

365
00:22:36,121 --> 00:22:40,259
TROY! I KNOW
YOU CAN HEAR ME, TROY.

366
00:22:40,259 --> 00:22:42,995
I KNOW YOU HAVE THE MAP.

367
00:22:42,995 --> 00:22:44,296
I WANT IT.

368
00:22:44,296 --> 00:22:46,999
JESSE "THE BODY" VENTURA
DUBBED HIS VOICE.

369
00:22:51,337 --> 00:22:54,039
WOW, AUNTIE SENT
HER JACK-BOOTED THUGS

370
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:56,575
TO MAKE HIM LUNCH.

371
00:23:03,382 --> 00:23:07,119
WE JUST WANT TO CUT
YOUR SUGAR-CANE CROP.

372
00:23:12,258 --> 00:23:15,294
YOU THUGS, DON’T RUN
WITH YOUR SCIMITARS.

373
00:23:16,795 --> 00:23:20,799
DAM, HE’S GOT A 10-SPEED.

374
00:23:20,799 --> 00:23:24,536
GET ON THE BANANA-SEAT BIKE,
AND GIVE CHASE.

375
00:23:24,536 --> 00:23:25,804
LET’S GET OUT OF HERE.

376
00:23:25,804 --> 00:23:29,241
HEY MAN, THANK YOUR SISTER
FOR SEWING OUR HOODS.

377
00:23:40,352 --> 00:23:41,887
[LAUGHTER]

378
00:23:41,887 --> 00:23:44,923
AND THEN THE DRUNK GUY SAYS,
I CAN’T HELP BEING AN IDIOT,

379
00:23:44,923 --> 00:23:46,325
I’M CANADIAN.

380
00:23:46,325 --> 00:23:47,927
[LAUGHTER]

381
00:23:47,927 --> 00:23:50,496
YOU’RE RIGHT,
THEY’RE SO PATHETIC, MIKE.

382
00:23:50,496 --> 00:23:51,864
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

383
00:23:51,864 --> 00:23:53,365
HUH?

384
00:23:53,365 --> 00:23:56,936
ENOUGH! THERE’S BEEN TOO MUCH
CANADA BASHING FOR FAR TOO LONG.

385
00:23:56,936 --> 00:23:58,971
I SAY NO MORE.

386
00:23:58,971 --> 00:24:01,073
DON’T YOU MEAN, NO MORE EH?

387
00:24:01,073 --> 00:24:02,374
- [LAUGHER]
- GOOD ONE, MAN.

388
00:24:02,374 --> 00:24:04,076
THEY ARE SO STUPID.

389
00:24:04,076 --> 00:24:05,277
STOP IT NOW.

390
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:07,079
INSTEAD LET US OFFER
OUR NORTHERN BROTHERS

391
00:24:07,079 --> 00:24:10,115
AND SISTERS
THIS SONG OF TRIBUTE.

392
00:24:10,115 --> 00:24:14,253
♪ OH, I WISH I WAS BACK
IN OLD CANADA ♪

393
00:24:14,253 --> 00:24:17,456
♪ A LAND WHICH I NEVER
SHALL LAMPOON ♪

394
00:24:17,456 --> 00:24:21,060
♪ HOW I PINE FOR THE ICE
COVERING LAKE MANITOBA ♪

395
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:24,063
♪ AND THE BEAUTY
THAT IS SASKATOON ♪

396
00:24:24,063 --> 00:24:25,397
I GOT ONE.

397
00:24:25,397 --> 00:24:28,133
♪ I WISH I WAS STUCK
IN THE HILLS OF ALBERTA ♪

398
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:31,637
♪ DRINKING BEER WITH SOME
BIG, DUMB GUY TRAPPING FUR ♪

399
00:24:31,637 --> 00:24:33,272
♪ AS HE SCRAPED
AND HE CHISELED ♪

400
00:24:33,272 --> 00:24:35,140
♪ ALL THE MOOSE DUNG
OFF HIS BOOTS ♪

401
00:24:35,140 --> 00:24:37,609
♪ I WOULD LEARN
THAT HE’S THE PRIME MINISTER ♪

402
00:24:37,609 --> 00:24:39,178
OH, STOP THAT.

403
00:24:39,178 --> 00:24:42,681
♪ OH, I WISH I WAS IN THE LAND
THAT GAVE US PETER JENNINGS ♪

404
00:24:42,681 --> 00:24:45,651
♪ ALANIS MORISSETTE,
MIKE MYERS TOO ♪

405
00:24:45,651 --> 00:24:47,920
♪ NO, I TAKE THAT BACK
I WOULDN’T GO THERE ♪

406
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:49,421
♪ EVEN IN YOU PAID ME ♪

407
00:24:49,421 --> 00:24:52,024
♪ OH, CANADA, YOU ARE A PLACE
I MUST ESCHEW ♪

408
00:24:52,024 --> 00:24:53,892
NOW THIS IS NOT IN THE SPIRIT
THAT I INTENDED.

409
00:24:53,892 --> 00:24:55,361
OH, COME ON. GIVE IN.

410
00:24:55,361 --> 00:24:58,530
I MEAN, AFTER ALL, THEY GAVE US
ED THE SOCK AND RUSH.

411
00:24:58,530 --> 00:25:00,599
YEAH, WHAT ARE YOU DEFENDING?
THEY’RE SUCH FEEBS.

412
00:25:00,599 --> 00:25:03,202
- OKAY, I’LL TRY.
- ALL RIGHT. GOOD MAN.

413
00:25:03,202 --> 00:25:07,339
♪ OH, I WISH I WAS BLOWING UP
PRINCE EDWARD ISLAND ♪

414
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:10,409
♪ GOING ON TO BOMB ONTARIO ♪

415
00:25:10,409 --> 00:25:13,879
♪ THE DESTRUCTION OF CANADA
AND ALL OF ITS CULTURE ♪

416
00:25:13,879 --> 00:25:16,849
♪ IS BY FAR
MY FAVORITE SCENARIO ♪

417
00:25:16,849 --> 00:25:18,584
OKAY, THAT’S A LITTLE STRONG.
YOU MIGHT WANT TO BACK IT DOWN.

418
00:25:18,584 --> 00:25:20,886
NO, NO YOU WERE RIGHT, MIKE.
THIS IS MUCH MORE FUN.

419
00:25:20,886 --> 00:25:22,488
♪ JUST WHERE THE HELL DOES
CANADA GET OFF ♪

420
00:25:22,488 --> 00:25:24,757
♪ SHARING A BORDER ♪

421
00:25:24,757 --> 00:25:27,092
♪ WITH COUNTRIES
FAR SUPERIOR TO IT? ♪

422
00:25:27,092 --> 00:25:28,360
YIKES.

423
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,295
♪ WHY YOU LOUSY, STINKIN’,
FRANCOPHONIC, ♪

424
00:25:30,295 --> 00:25:31,930
♪ BACON LOVING BASTARDS ♪

425
00:25:31,930 --> 00:25:33,966
♪ YOUR COUNTRY’S
JUST A GIANT PIECE OF-- ♪

426
00:25:33,966 --> 00:25:35,267
- WHOA, WHOA, WHOA, EASY!
- OKAY, I THINK THAT’S ENOUGH.

427
00:25:35,267 --> 00:25:37,469
I THINK WE GOING TO CAMBOT.
OKAY, THANKS.

428
00:25:37,469 --> 00:25:38,570
- ALL RIGHT.
- WOW.

429
00:25:38,570 --> 00:25:40,305
I HAVE NO
SENSE OF PROPORTION.

430
00:25:40,305 --> 00:25:42,474
I’M A DISGRACE TO MY UNIFORM.

431
00:25:42,474 --> 00:25:44,343
NO, THAT’S OKAY.
NOW, CALM DOWN.

432
00:25:44,343 --> 00:25:45,978
NOW, WE MUSTN’T HATE.
MUSTN’T HATE.

433
00:25:45,978 --> 00:25:47,479
AT LEAST SO OVERTLY.

434
00:25:47,479 --> 00:25:50,182
EXACTLY RIGHT. MUST DISGUISE
OUR HATE JUST A LITTLE.

435
00:25:50,182 --> 00:25:52,651
WE’LL BE RIGHT BACK.
SSH, SSH, IT’S OKAY NOW, DUDLEY.

436
00:25:52,651 --> 00:25:54,653
- CALM DOWN. CALM DOWN.
- PARDONNEZ-MOI.

437
00:25:54,653 --> 00:25:56,355
 PARDONNEZ-MOI. 

438
00:25:56,355 --> 00:25:58,290
♪♪

439
00:26:05,330 --> 00:26:08,567
SEVEN YEARS LATER.

440
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:10,969
DENTAL HYGIENIST OF THE WEEK.

441
00:26:16,375 --> 00:26:17,743
YEAH, ONCE HE GETS IT STARTED,

442
00:26:17,743 --> 00:26:19,378
HE’S GOING TO DRIVE IT
TO THE FRONT YARD,

443
00:26:19,378 --> 00:26:21,313
TAKE A COUPLE OF TIRES OFF,
AND LET IT RUST

444
00:26:21,313 --> 00:26:25,584
NEXT TO THE OLD FREEZER
SITTING ON THE FRONT LAWN.

445
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:27,586
AH.

446
00:26:27,586 --> 00:26:29,621
IN MY WORK
FOR A BLOODTHIRSTY CULT,

447
00:26:29,621 --> 00:26:32,224
I DEPEND ON MY GRAN TORINO.

448
00:26:32,224 --> 00:26:36,395
I THINK HIS MENACE IS UNDERCUT
BY THE "BABY ON BOARD" TAG.

449
00:26:39,731 --> 00:26:43,836
HEY, I THINK YOUR CAMERAMAN’S
STUCK IN THE DOOR.

450
00:26:43,836 --> 00:26:45,971
SEE?

451
00:26:49,107 --> 00:26:51,777
CAN YOU IMAGINE HOW MANY
POTATO OLé CONTAINERS

452
00:26:51,777 --> 00:26:54,480
ARE ON THE FLOOR OF THAT CAR?

453
00:26:56,215 --> 00:26:59,818
THIS MUSIC IS REALLY MORE SUITED
TO PLATE SPINNING.

454
00:26:59,818 --> 00:27:02,120
KIND OF A MAZURKA.

455
00:27:04,823 --> 00:27:08,293
I’M LOSING TRACK
OF THE CRAPPY VEHICLES HERE.

456
00:27:11,964 --> 00:27:15,567
CRANK THE MOLLY HATCHET
AND LET’S ROLL!

457
00:27:15,567 --> 00:27:16,902
 [RADIO CHATTER]

458
00:27:16,902 --> 00:27:20,405
I’M SHERRY.

459
00:27:20,405 --> 00:27:22,474
 THIS IS CAROL DOLAN,
 AND I’LL BE BACK.

460
00:27:22,474 --> 00:27:27,045
AW, NOW I HAVE TO
LISTEN TO AS IT HAPPENS.

461
00:27:27,045 --> 00:27:29,748
HONK! HONK! ON YOUR ASS!

462
00:27:31,917 --> 00:27:35,487
OH, I LOVE TRASH--
OW, OH, GOD.

463
00:27:38,190 --> 00:27:40,425
MAYBE IT’S THE CHEAP
CANADIAN GAS THEY’RE USING.

464
00:27:40,425 --> 00:27:43,161
JUST CAN’T GET UP ANY SPEED.

465
00:27:48,967 --> 00:27:51,503
DAMN YOU, PEEWEE!

466
00:27:55,040 --> 00:27:58,443
HI, I’M BILLY THE BUILDING.
[LAUGHS]

467
00:28:04,650 --> 00:28:06,752
UNFORTUNATELY,
THE TRUCK’S MAKING A DELIVERY

468
00:28:06,752 --> 00:28:09,221
RIGHT BACK TO THE CULT.

469
00:28:13,659 --> 00:28:15,227
WELL, LET’S JUST
GO GET SOME BULLWHIPS

470
00:28:15,227 --> 00:28:17,396
AND POSE FOR MAPPLETHORPE.

471
00:28:17,396 --> 00:28:19,031
YUP.

472
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:23,969
HUDDLED IN A PILE
OF DIRTY LAUNDRY,

473
00:28:23,969 --> 00:28:26,271
IT’S JUST LIKE HOME.

474
00:28:32,844 --> 00:28:35,914
IT SOUNDS LIKE
VIDEO-POKER MUSIC.

475
00:28:40,118 --> 00:28:41,386
AND THEY TAKE REFUGE

476
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:43,322
IN THE ANNE MURRAY
NATIONAL FOREST.

477
00:28:43,322 --> 00:28:45,724
BEAUTIFUL, ISN’T IT?

478
00:28:45,724 --> 00:28:48,327
I THINK HE’S
THE TIN DRUM KID.

479
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:56,802
HE’S THE KIND OF CLOWN
WHO PUTS $1.87 OF GAS

480
00:28:56,802 --> 00:28:59,304
IN HIS TRUCK.

481
00:28:59,304 --> 00:29:01,940
HELP ME, OH,
SAINT LARRY CSONKA.

482
00:29:05,577 --> 00:29:08,647
WELL, IT WENT FURTHER
THAN IT USUALLY DOES.

483
00:29:08,647 --> 00:29:11,383
LIKE A... [COUGHS]
ROCK.

484
00:29:15,287 --> 00:29:18,390
ANOTHER HUMAN BEING.
OH, I’M IN FOR A BEATING.

485
00:29:24,696 --> 00:29:25,998
WHAT THE HELL?

486
00:29:25,998 --> 00:29:28,700
I’VE ALWAYS BEEN
BACK HERE, REMEMBER?

487
00:29:28,700 --> 00:29:30,836
WHAT ARE YOU DOING
BACK THERE, KID?

488
00:29:30,836 --> 00:29:31,870
I...

489
00:29:31,870 --> 00:29:33,972
I’M LAUNDRY.

490
00:29:33,972 --> 00:29:35,140
I NEEDED A RIDE.

491
00:29:35,140 --> 00:29:37,442
IS HE A MAKEUPLESS CLOWN?

492
00:29:37,442 --> 00:29:38,477
WHY DON’T YOU GET IN THE CAB?

493
00:29:38,477 --> 00:29:39,578
IT’S MUCH
MORE COMFORTABLE THERE.

494
00:29:39,578 --> 00:29:42,447
ACTUALLY, I BET IT ISN’T.

495
00:29:50,155 --> 00:29:52,557
SO, UH, EH THEN, EH?

496
00:29:52,557 --> 00:29:53,659
[COUGHING]

497
00:29:53,659 --> 00:29:56,862
EH.

498
00:29:56,862 --> 00:29:59,297
DON’T YOU LOVE
OUR HEALTHCARE SYSTEM?

499
00:29:59,297 --> 00:30:01,099
HERE, PUT THIS ON.

500
00:30:01,099 --> 00:30:03,669
- IT’S MADE OF LUNCH MEAT.
- THANKS.

501
00:30:10,208 --> 00:30:12,277
KNOW ANYTHING ABOUT MOTORS?

502
00:30:12,277 --> 00:30:15,080
NO, SIR. NOT REALLY.

503
00:30:15,080 --> 00:30:17,849
 I KNOW ALL THE SONGS FROM
 ONCE UPON A MATTRESS THOUGH.

504
00:30:17,849 --> 00:30:19,618
LET’S HAVE A LOOK.

505
00:30:19,618 --> 00:30:21,353
ARE YOU GONNA BE A MOUNTIE
OR A FISHING GUIDE

506
00:30:21,353 --> 00:30:23,689
WHEN YOU GROW UP?

507
00:30:23,689 --> 00:30:26,391
- WHERE ARE YOU HEADING?
- LIQUOR STORE.

508
00:30:26,391 --> 00:30:29,227
LOOKS LIKE
I’M HEADING NOWHERE.

509
00:30:29,227 --> 00:30:33,231
I SEE THE PROBLEM.
THE GAS LINE’S LOOSE.

510
00:30:33,231 --> 00:30:34,466
YOU’RE GETTING BEHIND
THE STEERING WHEEL,

511
00:30:34,466 --> 00:30:35,867
AND CRANK HER OVER
WHEN I TELL YOU.

512
00:30:35,867 --> 00:30:38,670
HE’S WEARING FASHIONS
BY MAC DAVIS.

513
00:30:43,141 --> 00:30:47,112
I’LL JUST, UH,
POUR MY GARBAGE IN HERE.

514
00:30:47,112 --> 00:30:48,880
NOW!

515
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:51,083
KABOOM!

516
00:30:51,083 --> 00:30:53,752
DIDN’T BARBARA MANDRELL
HAVE HAIR LIKE HIS AT ONE POINT?

517
00:30:53,752 --> 00:30:55,454
I THINK SO. YUP, YUP.

518
00:30:55,454 --> 00:30:58,757
PUT THE PEDAL
ALL THE WAY DOWN.

519
00:30:58,757 --> 00:31:01,093
HM, DARE I?

520
00:31:01,093 --> 00:31:03,395
[ENGINE STRUGGLING]

521
00:31:06,965 --> 00:31:11,403
BETTER CHECK THIS OIL HERE.
YEP, 10W-30.

522
00:31:11,403 --> 00:31:12,604
[SIZZLING]

523
00:31:12,604 --> 00:31:15,974
OOH, HIS HAIR’S ON FIRE.

524
00:31:15,974 --> 00:31:17,943
KEEP HER GOING, KID!

525
00:31:20,612 --> 00:31:22,848
OKAY, BRING THE BRATS OUT.

526
00:31:25,584 --> 00:31:26,718
[LAUGHS]

527
00:31:26,718 --> 00:31:29,421
OUTWITTED MY TRUCK AGAIN!

528
00:31:33,125 --> 00:31:35,327
- WHAT’S YOUR NAME, LADDIE?
- TROY McGREGGOR.

529
00:31:35,327 --> 00:31:37,462
I’M ROWSDOWER.

530
00:31:37,462 --> 00:31:38,730
ZAP ROWSDOWER.

531
00:31:38,730 --> 00:31:42,367
WELL, MY NAME
IS BILL SHTINKWATER.

532
00:31:42,367 --> 00:31:44,770
ROWSDOWER-MOBILE AWAY!

533
00:31:44,770 --> 00:31:48,940
AND TOGETHER THEY FOUGHT CRIME
THROUGHOUT SOUTHWESTERN ALBERTA!

534
00:31:51,810 --> 00:31:56,715
SO, ROWSDOWER,
IS THAT A STUPID NAME, OR...?

535
00:31:56,715 --> 00:32:00,952
- UH, FILL HER UP.
- YUP.

536
00:32:00,952 --> 00:32:03,088
YOU STAY HERE AND I’LL GET YOU
A CHOCOLATE BAR, OKAY?

537
00:32:03,088 --> 00:32:04,823
- THANKS.
- BUY ME ANYTHING IN THERE

538
00:32:04,823 --> 00:32:07,626
WITH LARRY CSONKA ON IT.
I’LL PAY FOR IT.

539
00:32:13,799 --> 00:32:16,768
SHOOT, I’M IN CANADA.

540
00:32:24,075 --> 00:32:25,343
OPERATOR, GIVE ME THE POLICE.

541
00:32:25,343 --> 00:32:28,713
AND THE COPS PICK UP
THEIR ZAP ROWSDOWER HOTLINE.

542
00:32:31,449 --> 00:32:33,552
YES, OFFICE, I FOUND THIS KID
IN THE BACK OF MY TRUCK.

543
00:32:33,552 --> 00:32:37,889
AND PLAY IN THE FRONT SEAT.

544
00:32:37,889 --> 00:32:40,992
♪ ROLL ON, BIG MAMA,
THE HIGHWAY ♪

545
00:32:40,992 --> 00:32:42,727
HOW SHOULD I KNOW? ASK HIM.

546
00:32:42,727 --> 00:32:44,796
EW, GOTTA GET
THIS DEAD WOODCHUCK OUT

547
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:46,865
FROM UNDER THE SEAT.
EW, POOEY.

548
00:32:46,865 --> 00:32:49,100
LOOK, YOU’RE GOING TO
SEND SOMEONE TO PICK HIM UP?

549
00:32:52,304 --> 00:32:54,306
WHAT DO THEY THINK
THEY’RE IN IDAHO?

550
00:32:57,142 --> 00:33:01,446
HEY, I’VE GOT 89 CENTS
WORTH OF CANS BACK THERE!

551
00:33:01,446 --> 00:33:04,249
ZAP ACTIONS-DOWER.

552
00:33:07,953 --> 00:33:09,087
[GUNSHOTS]

553
00:33:09,087 --> 00:33:12,324
MY HOOD WICKS MOISTURE
FROM MY FACE.

554
00:33:16,795 --> 00:33:21,333
UM, EAT MY DUST.
I DON’T KNOW.

555
00:33:21,333 --> 00:33:24,236
DO THESE PANTS
GO WITH THIS SWEATER?

556
00:33:29,507 --> 00:33:32,811
YOU KNOW, HE BLENDS IN.
HE LOOKS LIKE A SACK OF GARBAGE.

557
00:33:32,811 --> 00:33:37,148
MM-HM.

558
00:33:37,148 --> 00:33:39,684
[GRUNTS]

559
00:33:42,687 --> 00:33:46,558
THIS IS NO TIME FOR ZYMURGY.

560
00:33:46,558 --> 00:33:50,128
HEY, JUST DON’T SHOOT AT ME
FOR A COUPLE OF MINUTES, OKAY?
THANKS.

561
00:33:54,933 --> 00:33:58,203
IF THIS DOESN’T WORK,
I’LL THROW BALLS OF CARP DOUGH.

562
00:34:04,809 --> 00:34:07,846
YOU WANT US
TO PICK THAT UP FOR YOU?

563
00:34:12,817 --> 00:34:15,787
I KNEW THERE WAS AN UPSIDE
TO BEING AN ALCOHOLIC.

564
00:34:17,589 --> 00:34:20,492
CAN YOU TAKE THOSE
TO RECYCLING? THANKS.

565
00:34:24,963 --> 00:34:27,332
CANADIAN MANNIX!

566
00:34:30,201 --> 00:34:33,939
UH, SO, YOU WANNA
HIT THE BRAKES, THERE, OR NOT?

567
00:34:38,944 --> 00:34:40,845
OH, I’M SO RELAXED RIGHT NOW.

568
00:34:40,845 --> 00:34:42,781
♪♪

569
00:34:48,019 --> 00:34:50,422
ROWSDOWER, I CAN EXPLAIN.

570
00:34:50,422 --> 00:34:52,190
THOSE MEN
WERE TRYING TO KILL ME.

571
00:34:52,190 --> 00:34:55,193
YEAH, TELL IT
TO MY ACID-WASHED JEANS.

572
00:34:58,229 --> 00:35:00,365
DO YOU HAVE ANY IDEA
WHAT KIND OF PEOPLE
YOU’RE DEALING WITH?

573
00:35:00,365 --> 00:35:02,233
THEY’RE FROM SASKATCHEWAN.

574
00:35:02,233 --> 00:35:04,402
NO.

575
00:35:04,402 --> 00:35:07,172
- IT’S A CULT.
- THEY WORSHIP BLUE OYSTERS.

576
00:35:07,172 --> 00:35:09,407
THEY WANT TO RULE THE WORLD.

577
00:35:09,407 --> 00:35:12,277
HOW DO YOU KNOW THAT?

578
00:35:12,277 --> 00:35:13,511
I’VE BEEN AROUND, KID.

579
00:35:13,511 --> 00:35:16,581
- AND I’VE BEEN A SQUARE KID.
- NO.

580
00:35:16,581 --> 00:35:18,216
TELL ME MORE ABOUT THEM.

581
00:35:18,216 --> 00:35:19,718
THEIR FACES
ARE LUMPY AND WHISKERED.

582
00:35:19,718 --> 00:35:22,854
OH, WAIT, THAT’S ME.

583
00:35:22,854 --> 00:35:24,422
THE RACE
RULED THIS LAND ONCE.

584
00:35:24,422 --> 00:35:26,257
THEY RULED THIS ONE ACRE
FOR ABOUT A WEEK.

585
00:35:26,257 --> 00:35:27,325
NOBODY KNEW.

586
00:35:27,325 --> 00:35:31,596
THE RACE
OF THE ZIOX CIVILIZATION.

587
00:35:31,596 --> 00:35:34,199
- ZIOX?
- WASN’T THAT A SANDWICH COOKIE?

588
00:35:34,199 --> 00:35:38,403
MY DAD WROTE ABOUT THEM.

589
00:35:38,403 --> 00:35:40,739
BTO WAS SUCH
A GREAT BAND, MAN.

590
00:35:40,739 --> 00:35:43,441
LOOK.

591
00:35:43,441 --> 00:35:45,877
I’M ABOUT TO PUKE, KID.
YOU MIGHT WANT TO CLEAR OUT.

592
00:35:45,877 --> 00:35:48,013
LOOK AT THE WRITING.

593
00:35:48,013 --> 00:35:49,414
IT’S ANCIENT.

594
00:35:49,414 --> 00:35:52,417
OLD AS THE CRUMBS
IN YOUR MOUSTACHE.

595
00:35:52,417 --> 00:35:55,220
WHERE DOES THIS LEAD TO?

596
00:35:55,220 --> 00:35:57,689
WELL, NOBODY KNOWS
FOR SURE...

597
00:35:57,689 --> 00:36:00,191
EXCEPT MY DAD, BUT UM...

598
00:36:00,191 --> 00:36:01,960
I DISAPPOINTED HIM.

599
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:04,129
HE WAS KILLED
SEVEN YEARS AGO.

600
00:36:04,129 --> 00:36:06,431
AND I WANT TO KNOW
WHY HE DIED.

601
00:36:06,431 --> 00:36:08,800
THIS MAP IS MY ONLY LEAD.

602
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:11,202
YEAH, HANG ON. [BURPS]

603
00:36:11,202 --> 00:36:12,570
GO TO SLEEP, KID.

604
00:36:12,570 --> 00:36:14,072
I’M TAKING YOU HOME
IN THE MORNING.

605
00:36:14,072 --> 00:36:17,676
OH, I THINK HE’S TAKING HIM HOME
IN THE MORNING. YEAH, YEAH.

606
00:36:17,676 --> 00:36:19,044
YUP.

607
00:36:22,247 --> 00:36:23,848
ROWSDOWER?

608
00:36:23,848 --> 00:36:25,917
[LAUGHING]

609
00:36:25,917 --> 00:36:26,951
YEAH?

610
00:36:26,951 --> 00:36:30,221
WHY DO I FEEL LIKE
HAVING HAGGIS?

611
00:36:30,221 --> 00:36:32,624
- HAVE YOU ALWAYS BEEN A--
- HOPELESS DRUNK.

612
00:36:32,624 --> 00:36:35,527
DRIFTER?

613
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:39,330
ROWSDOWER, COULD YOU
PUT OUT MY HEAD?

614
00:36:39,330 --> 00:36:40,932
NO.

615
00:36:40,932 --> 00:36:42,033
OH.

616
00:36:42,033 --> 00:36:43,535
WELL, WHAT WERE YOU BEFORE?

617
00:36:43,535 --> 00:36:48,073
WELL, I USED TO GIVE PLASMA.
YOU MIGHT KNOW ME FROM THAT.

618
00:36:48,073 --> 00:36:52,510
- I WAS A--
-  A CHIPPENDALES DANCER.

619
00:36:52,510 --> 00:36:55,480
A BUSINESSMAN.

620
00:36:55,480 --> 00:36:56,915
WHAT HAPPENED?

621
00:36:56,915 --> 00:37:00,018
WELL, I SWITCHED TO BEATING UP
ANNOYING KIDS WITH BEER BOTTLES.

622
00:37:07,058 --> 00:37:08,326
GO TO SLEEP, KID.

623
00:37:08,326 --> 00:37:12,397
YOU’RE HARSHING MY BUZZ.

624
00:37:12,397 --> 00:37:16,601
HUH, NOW IS THIS TOUCHING
OR BORING? I CAN’T...

625
00:37:16,601 --> 00:37:20,071
REALLY...

626
00:37:20,071 --> 00:37:21,906
ROWSDOWER.

627
00:37:25,610 --> 00:37:28,746
NOW THAT IS A DARLING
MAXI SKIRT.

628
00:37:31,616 --> 00:37:36,121
[YAWNS]
ROWSDOWER.

629
00:37:36,121 --> 00:37:39,324
WOW, I DREAMT I WAS STUCK
WITH A CHUNKY BACKWOODS LOSER

630
00:37:39,324 --> 00:37:42,393
NAMED ROWSDOWER-- AAH!

631
00:37:42,393 --> 00:37:45,730
[COUGHS] I THINK
MY VOICE CHANGED OVERNIGHT.

632
00:37:48,766 --> 00:37:50,668
GOOD MORNING.

633
00:37:52,871 --> 00:37:56,508
SO YOU GONNA GET US
OUT OF HERE?

634
00:37:56,508 --> 00:37:57,575
I’LL GET US OUT OF HERE.

635
00:37:57,575 --> 00:38:01,146
THEN WE’LL STALL
50 YARDS DOWN THE LINE.

636
00:38:01,146 --> 00:38:05,583
WHY WERE YOU GOING TO
TURN ME OVER TO THE COPS?

637
00:38:05,583 --> 00:38:07,352
BECAUSE I LIKE TO KEEP
MY NOSE CLEAN.

638
00:38:07,352 --> 00:38:09,220
MY BODY SUFFERS
FOR IT, BUT...

639
00:38:09,220 --> 00:38:11,656
HELPING A RUNAWAY KID
CAN GET ME IN BIG TROUBLE.

640
00:38:11,656 --> 00:38:14,659
I’D LOVE FOR YOU TO MEET
THE PEOPLE IN MY YOUTH GROUP.

641
00:38:17,762 --> 00:38:20,131
ROWSDOWER?

642
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:22,433
HAVE YOU EVER BATHED?

643
00:38:22,433 --> 00:38:25,303
WILL YOU HELP ME FIND
WHAT’S BEHIND THE MAP?

644
00:38:25,303 --> 00:38:28,873
OH, I DON’T GO
MAP FINDING BEHINDING.

645
00:38:28,873 --> 00:38:30,475
YOU SHOULD BE IN SCHOOL.

646
00:38:30,475 --> 00:38:33,945
NOT RUNNING AROUND
HUNTING DOWN LOST CIVILIZATIONS.

647
00:38:33,945 --> 00:38:36,514
BESIDES, THE MAP
COULD BE A FAKE.

648
00:38:36,514 --> 00:38:38,283
A FANTASY OF YOUR OLD MAN’S.

649
00:38:38,283 --> 00:38:40,585
WHY DO YOU THINK THOSE MEN
WERE FOLLOWING US YESTERDAY?

650
00:38:40,585 --> 00:38:42,687
AH, THEY THOUGHT I WAS THAT GUY
FROM  DUE SOUTH. 

651
00:38:42,687 --> 00:38:44,489
DON’T YOU SEE?

652
00:38:44,489 --> 00:38:46,124
THEY WERE AFTER THIS.

653
00:38:46,124 --> 00:38:49,794
ROWSDOWER’S GOT ONE
OF SCREENDOM’S BEST REAR ENDS.

654
00:38:49,794 --> 00:38:52,764
MM-HMM.

655
00:38:52,764 --> 00:38:55,166
YOU GIVE ME A HAND NOW, KID.

656
00:38:55,166 --> 00:38:57,669
ROWSDOWER!

657
00:39:04,943 --> 00:39:07,812
DO YOU KNOW HOW FAST
YOU WERE GOING, ROWSDOWER?

658
00:39:10,215 --> 00:39:14,619
COME ON.

659
00:39:14,619 --> 00:39:16,287
COME ON, BABY.
DON’T LET ME DOWN.

660
00:39:16,287 --> 00:39:18,756
I WON’T, ROWSDOWER.

661
00:39:18,756 --> 00:39:22,660
[ENGINE TURNS OVER]
WATCH OUT, KID.

662
00:39:22,660 --> 00:39:27,065
ROWSDOWER-ER-ER-ER.

663
00:39:27,065 --> 00:39:29,667
DAMN.

664
00:39:29,667 --> 00:39:33,137
YOU’RE GOING TO DRIVE
WHILE I PUSH AT THE FRONT.

665
00:39:33,137 --> 00:39:34,505
START OUT SLOW.

666
00:39:34,505 --> 00:39:36,674
WHEN YOU GET UP SOME SPEED,
FLOOR HER. GOT IT?

667
00:39:36,674 --> 00:39:38,042
AND I’D LIKE
TO THANK DAN AYKROYD

668
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:40,345
FOR DOING THAT LAST LINE.

669
00:39:44,115 --> 00:39:47,886
GO!

670
00:39:47,886 --> 00:39:50,521
FUDGE.

671
00:39:50,521 --> 00:39:53,258
CHILDREN AND PREGNANT WOMEN
SHOULD NOT WATCH THIS SCENE.

672
00:39:53,258 --> 00:39:54,826
YOU KNOW, IN FACT, NO ONE
SHOULD REALLY WATCH

673
00:39:54,826 --> 00:39:55,893
ANY OF THESE SCENES.

674
00:39:55,893 --> 00:39:57,328
- YEAH, YOU’RE RIGHT.
- I AGREE.

675
00:40:00,832 --> 00:40:02,200
THIS IS LIKE
WHEN OUR NURSING HOME

676
00:40:02,200 --> 00:40:04,869
VOLUNTEER BUS BROKE DOWN.

677
00:40:04,869 --> 00:40:07,105
[EXPLOSION]
WOW!

678
00:40:07,105 --> 00:40:09,874
SOUNDS LIKE ROWSDOWER’S HEART
JUST EXPLODED.

679
00:40:13,211 --> 00:40:15,380
[HEAVY PANTING]

680
00:40:15,380 --> 00:40:17,282
I DON’T THINK
THAT WAS A VERY GOOD IDEA.

681
00:40:17,282 --> 00:40:18,917
SHUT UP.

682
00:40:18,917 --> 00:40:20,518
WE’RE IN FOR A LONG WALK.

683
00:40:20,518 --> 00:40:23,021
- WE’RE GONNA WALK?
- WELL, IT’S NOT MY FAULT!

684
00:40:23,021 --> 00:40:26,724
YOU’RE THE ONE
THAT GOT US INTO THIS MESS.

685
00:40:26,724 --> 00:40:28,726
YOU STAY HERE
WHILE I GO GET US SOME WATER.

686
00:40:28,726 --> 00:40:32,697
- I’LL GO.
- CAN YOU CARRY ME?

687
00:40:32,697 --> 00:40:34,265
CANTEEN’S IN THE CAB.

688
00:40:34,265 --> 00:40:37,235
AND THE CAB’S DOWN
AT COLUMBUS AND 77th.

689
00:40:43,574 --> 00:40:47,245
AND IF YOU FIND A PACKAGE STORE,
GET ME SOME YUKON JACK.

690
00:40:54,185 --> 00:40:56,788
THANKS FOR THE RIDE, MISTER.

691
00:40:59,023 --> 00:41:01,893
WELL, I TRY TO WORK OUT,
BUT IT JUST GETS HARD.

692
00:41:07,932 --> 00:41:10,635
♪ GETTING WATER
FOR ROWSDOWER ♪

693
00:41:10,635 --> 00:41:13,471
♪ ROWSDOWER WANTS ME
TO GET WATER FOR HIM ♪

694
00:41:13,471 --> 00:41:16,240
[SNIFFS]
EW, NATURE SMELLS.

695
00:41:16,240 --> 00:41:18,109
MIKE, IS THERE ANY WAY
I COULD HOP INTO THE MOVIE

696
00:41:18,109 --> 00:41:19,410
AND DUMP THIS KID’S BOOKS?

697
00:41:19,410 --> 00:41:21,713
OH, I ONLY WISH.

698
00:41:21,713 --> 00:41:24,582
SOMEBODY COVERED
THEIR TOMATO PLANTS.

699
00:41:29,754 --> 00:41:32,957
LET’S SEE WHAT MY CAP’N CRUNCH
TREASURE MAP SAYS.

700
00:41:36,928 --> 00:41:39,097
[GROWLS]

701
00:41:42,066 --> 00:41:45,036
THE THREE BAGUETTES.

702
00:41:45,036 --> 00:41:48,072
[GRUNTS]

703
00:41:50,908 --> 00:41:54,545
♪ ROWSDOWER, ROWSDOWER,
ROWSE-A-ROWSE-A-ROWSEDOWER ♪

704
00:41:54,545 --> 00:41:56,381
♪ BOWSE-A-BOWSE-A-BOWESDOWER ♪

705
00:41:56,381 --> 00:41:58,182
♪ SABIDI-SABIDI-SOWSDOWER ♪

706
00:41:58,182 --> 00:41:59,884
♪ BIPPITY-BOPPITY-BOWSEDOWER ♪

707
00:41:59,884 --> 00:42:02,520
♪ BOPPITY-DOPPITY-DOWER-ROWSE ♪

708
00:42:02,520 --> 00:42:04,122
♪ DOWER ♪

709
00:42:06,691 --> 00:42:09,694
SOMEBODY’S BREAKING
SHREDDED-WHEAT BISCUITS.

710
00:42:13,598 --> 00:42:16,000
OKAY, I DROPPED THE CANTEEN,
AND I GOT LOST.

711
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:17,702
RIGHT ON SCHEDULE.

712
00:42:17,702 --> 00:42:20,038
AH, NEXT I HAVE TO FALL,
BREAK MY ANKLE,

713
00:42:20,038 --> 00:42:22,874
BE ATTACKED BY COYOTES,
AND BURIED BY A BEAR.

714
00:42:22,874 --> 00:42:25,576
[HOWLING]

715
00:42:30,648 --> 00:42:33,951
TAKE A LEFT AT THE TREE.
THAT HELPS!

716
00:42:35,686 --> 00:42:37,622
♪♪

717
00:42:43,928 --> 00:42:45,496
BAD NEWS, LOSERS.

718
00:42:45,496 --> 00:42:46,864
WE WON’T BE IN TODAY

719
00:42:46,864 --> 00:42:49,934
BECAUSE BOBO ATE A BAD CAN
OF CANADIAN BACON,

720
00:42:49,934 --> 00:42:51,736
AND HE CAME DOWN
WITH HOCKEY HAIR,

721
00:42:51,736 --> 00:42:54,005
AND NOW WE’VE ALL GOT IT.

722
00:42:54,005 --> 00:42:56,240
LADY? LADY.

723
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:58,810
CAN I WATCH POWER RANGERS?

724
00:43:00,578 --> 00:43:02,613
WELL GEE, PEARL,
THAT’S TOO BAD.

725
00:43:02,613 --> 00:43:04,449
I GUESS THAT MEANS
IT’S CONTAGIOUS.

726
00:43:04,449 --> 00:43:06,751
OH, I’M SURE YOU GUYS
WILL BE FINE.

727
00:43:06,751 --> 00:43:08,386
I MEAN, WE LIVE WITH THE APE,

728
00:43:08,386 --> 00:43:11,022
SO WHEN HE GETS HOCKEY HAIR,
WE ALL GET HOCKEY HAIR.

729
00:43:11,022 --> 00:43:12,857
DON’T WORRY.

730
00:43:12,857 --> 00:43:16,627
THE-- THE DOCTOR SAYS
I HAVE TO HAVE MORE WHOPPERS

731
00:43:16,627 --> 00:43:19,530
AND MALTED MILK BALLS.

732
00:43:19,530 --> 00:43:22,133
YES, YES, DEAR.

733
00:43:22,133 --> 00:43:26,003
OH, FOR CRYING--
IT’S AN AIRBORNE VIRUS. SHEESH.

734
00:43:26,003 --> 00:43:28,072
MIKE, WHAT’S YOUR DEAL?
HOW COME YOU DON’T HAVE IT?

735
00:43:28,072 --> 00:43:32,376
OH, I HAD IT ONCE ALREADY
FROM 1982 TO 1992.

736
00:43:32,376 --> 00:43:34,378
ONCE YOU GET IT ONCE,
YOU CAN’T GET IT AGAIN.

737
00:43:34,378 --> 00:43:35,613
HUH.

738
00:43:35,613 --> 00:43:39,417
OH, NO.
YOU GUYS GOT IT TOO, HUH?

739
00:43:39,417 --> 00:43:42,620
WELL, THE BEST THING IS TO
JUST LET IT RUN ITS COURSE.

740
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:45,056
WELL, I THINK IT’S GREAT!

741
00:43:45,056 --> 00:43:47,325
I’VE NEVER FELT SO MASCULINE.

742
00:43:47,325 --> 00:43:49,594
I FEEL LIKE GUY LAFLEUR.

743
00:43:49,594 --> 00:43:53,998
IT’S TIME...
FOR MY HOURLY BEN AND JERRY’S.

744
00:43:55,933 --> 00:43:58,669
HUH, I HAVE THIS INTENSE
CRAVING FOR ZUBAZ.

745
00:43:58,669 --> 00:44:00,571
YEAH, YOU’RE GONNA GET THAT.
[ALARM BUZZES]

746
00:44:00,571 --> 00:44:03,508
- OH, THE MOVIE’S PLAYING.
- OH, SHERRY!

747
00:44:14,085 --> 00:44:17,188
- WHOA, WOOZY.
- SORRY, YOU GUYS.

748
00:44:17,188 --> 00:44:18,222
TROY!

749
00:44:18,222 --> 00:44:21,993
IT’S THE CANADIAN NICK NOLTE.

750
00:44:21,993 --> 00:44:23,494
TROY, WHERE ARE YOU?

751
00:44:23,494 --> 00:44:26,097
MR. AIKMAN!

752
00:44:26,097 --> 00:44:27,598
HEY, MISTER,
HAVE YOU SEEN ROWSDOWER?

753
00:44:27,598 --> 00:44:28,733
AH, HEY.

754
00:44:28,733 --> 00:44:31,836
- OVER HERE.
- WHAT?

755
00:44:34,805 --> 00:44:36,274
LOOK WHAT I FOUND.

756
00:44:36,274 --> 00:44:39,243
WHAT IS IT?

757
00:44:39,243 --> 00:44:41,245
IT’S A TUNNEL.

758
00:44:41,245 --> 00:44:42,580
YEAH, RIGHT.

759
00:44:42,580 --> 00:44:45,683
THAT IS A CLASSIC
ROWSDOWERISM.

760
00:44:47,685 --> 00:44:50,221
A BUG! YUCK!

761
00:44:58,729 --> 00:45:01,499
YOU’RE GOING TO THROW ME
DOWN THERE, AREN’T YOU?

762
00:45:05,236 --> 00:45:08,706
YEAH, NOT MATTER WHERE HE GOES,
HE FINDS A BASEMENT TO DWELL IN.

763
00:45:11,909 --> 00:45:15,780
EXCUSE ME.

764
00:45:15,780 --> 00:45:18,816
- WOW.
- THESE ARE REALLY CHEAP SETS.

765
00:45:20,685 --> 00:45:24,121
[LIGHTER FLICKS]

766
00:45:24,121 --> 00:45:26,257
THIS TUNNEL MUST HAVE BEEN DUG
HUNDREDS OF YEARS AGO.

767
00:45:26,257 --> 00:45:27,625
I SENSED THAT WITH MY HAIR.

768
00:45:27,625 --> 00:45:29,260
MY HAIR IS AN ELABORATE
NETWORK OF NERVES

769
00:45:29,260 --> 00:45:32,163
CONSTANTLY PROCESSING
INFORMATION.

770
00:45:33,931 --> 00:45:35,433
THIS TUNNEL IS ON THE MAP.

771
00:45:35,433 --> 00:45:38,336
HUH?

772
00:45:38,336 --> 00:45:40,972
I WAS RIGHT.

773
00:45:40,972 --> 00:45:42,273
THE MAP IS REAL.

774
00:45:42,273 --> 00:45:43,641
MAP ISRAEL?

775
00:45:43,641 --> 00:45:46,344
I BELIEVE ISRAEL HAS BEEN
FAIRLY WELL MAPPED ALREADY.

776
00:45:46,344 --> 00:45:49,347
STOP.

777
00:45:49,347 --> 00:45:52,016
IT’S AN EVIL PORKY PIG.

778
00:45:57,421 --> 00:45:59,824
THE PUKING BUDDHA.

779
00:45:59,824 --> 00:46:04,028
BLECH, I HATE-- WHAT IS THAT?
I HAVE HAIR IN MY MOUTH. BLECH.

780
00:46:07,265 --> 00:46:09,934
WHOA, NOT THERE, KID.
SENSITIVE AREA.

781
00:46:12,770 --> 00:46:15,806
NEVER CLIMB
IN PEOPLE YOU DON’T KNOW.

782
00:46:18,309 --> 00:46:19,877
TROY?

783
00:46:19,877 --> 00:46:23,381
ARE YOU DEAD,
BECAUSE IF YOU ARE,
I’M GONNA TAKE OFF.

784
00:46:28,552 --> 00:46:32,189
FIREWOOD FOR SALE.

785
00:46:32,189 --> 00:46:35,226
I GUESS THEY THOUGHT HE WAS
A BABY HARP-SEAL OR SOMETHING.

786
00:46:41,465 --> 00:46:44,935
THE JUST-ABOUT-TO-SNEEZE GOD.

787
00:46:52,009 --> 00:46:53,144
WOW!

788
00:46:53,144 --> 00:46:55,846
I REALLY DON’T UNDERSTAND.

789
00:46:59,283 --> 00:47:02,787
YOU TRESPASSED
ON CHARLTON HESTON’S PLACE.

790
00:47:04,655 --> 00:47:07,491
WE BAGGED OUR OWN HEADS
AND SAVED!

791
00:47:08,793 --> 00:47:11,395
- GIVE UP YOUR HOCKEY HAIR!
- NEVER!

792
00:47:11,395 --> 00:47:13,964
YOU...

793
00:47:13,964 --> 00:47:15,232
YOU.

794
00:47:15,232 --> 00:47:18,169
SO YOU’VE NOT
FORGOTTEN ME, ROWSDOWER.

795
00:47:18,169 --> 00:47:20,204
WE MEET AGAIN.

796
00:47:20,204 --> 00:47:22,573
FOR THE FINAL TIME,
I’M AFRAID.

797
00:47:22,573 --> 00:47:25,342
RED GROOMS’ DRACULA.

798
00:47:28,779 --> 00:47:31,449
MY HAWKWIND
ALBUM COVER WILL HELP.

799
00:47:33,284 --> 00:47:36,053
NOPE, NOTHIN’.
I DON’T GET IT.

800
00:47:37,755 --> 00:47:41,992
COME ON, KID.
GIVE US A HARDY "ROWSDOWER."

801
00:47:41,992 --> 00:47:45,129
- DAD!
- THAT’S MY FAVORITE
JACK LEMMON MOVIE.

802
00:47:45,129 --> 00:47:47,665
YOU WERE HERE.

803
00:47:47,665 --> 00:47:49,400
WEREN’T YOU?

804
00:47:49,400 --> 00:47:52,136
WHERE’S THE BOY?

805
00:47:52,136 --> 00:47:53,304
COULD YOU SQUAT DOWN?

806
00:47:53,304 --> 00:47:55,039
I WAS TRYING TO GET YOU
IN THE FACE ACTUALLY.

807
00:47:55,039 --> 00:47:57,775
- THE BOY, ROWSDOWER.
- THE BOY.

808
00:47:57,775 --> 00:47:59,777
HE WENT INTO
THE CAVE WITH YOU.

809
00:47:59,777 --> 00:48:02,813
HE HAS THE MAP. I WANT IT.

810
00:48:02,813 --> 00:48:04,415
I DON’T KNOW!

811
00:48:04,415 --> 00:48:06,817
LOOK INTO YOUR HEART, EH?

812
00:48:08,753 --> 00:48:11,889
WE’RE GOING TO MAKE YOU DRINK
SOMETHING OTHER THAN BEER.

813
00:48:13,791 --> 00:48:17,261
IT’S A CULT THAT WORSHIPS
GEORGIA O’KEEFFE.

814
00:48:22,032 --> 00:48:26,036
HEY, LOOK, MILK DUDS!
THEY NEVER GO BAD!

815
00:48:29,774 --> 00:48:32,309
HIS ARM SINKS IN
UP TO THE ELBOW.

816
00:48:34,345 --> 00:48:36,747
NOW GIVE ME YOUR LUNCH MONEY.

817
00:48:39,283 --> 00:48:41,886
LOOK AT THAT.
LOOK WHAT YOU DID. LOOK!

818
00:48:45,556 --> 00:48:48,559
HE COULD EASILY BE
IN LYNARD SKYNARD.

819
00:48:48,559 --> 00:48:50,094
YOU DON’T CONTROL ME.

820
00:48:50,094 --> 00:48:53,597
THIS HAS CONTROLLED
YOUR ENTIRE LIFE,
YOU DRUNKEN FOOL.

821
00:48:53,597 --> 00:48:57,168
- HEY, BRA STRAP.
- YOU’RE CRAZY.

822
00:48:57,168 --> 00:48:59,503
NO, I’M NOT CRAZY.

823
00:48:59,503 --> 00:49:02,006
I SHALL SEE THE WORLD RULED

824
00:49:02,006 --> 00:49:05,009
BY THE ONLY RACE
THAT WAS CREATED IN PERFECTION.

825
00:49:05,009 --> 00:49:06,477
- MM-HM.
- HUH?

826
00:49:06,477 --> 00:49:08,979
THEY’LL BE NO PLACE
FOR THE WEAK.

827
00:49:08,979 --> 00:49:11,582
THE UGLY.

828
00:49:11,582 --> 00:49:13,818
VERMIN LIKE YOU.

829
00:49:13,818 --> 00:49:15,052
GO TO HELL!

830
00:49:15,052 --> 00:49:17,955
OR AT LEAST EDMONTON!

831
00:49:17,955 --> 00:49:20,291
OUR DAY OF CONQUEST
IS ONCOMING.

832
00:49:20,291 --> 00:49:23,594
I’M SORRY, WHAT DID YOU SAY
ABOUT BURTON CUMMINGS?

833
00:49:23,594 --> 00:49:25,462
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

834
00:49:25,462 --> 00:49:27,498
THAT IS WHY YOU CAME BACK,
ISN’T IT?

835
00:49:27,498 --> 00:49:30,401
YOU LEFT YOUR ALBUMS
AT MY PLACE.

836
00:49:30,401 --> 00:49:32,336
ON A DAY SOON,

837
00:49:32,336 --> 00:49:36,073
AN HOUR OF DARKNESS,

838
00:49:36,073 --> 00:49:38,776
OUR GOD WILL ACCEPT
A HUMAN SACRIFICE.

839
00:49:38,776 --> 00:49:40,311
OR YOU. I’M KIDDING.

840
00:49:40,311 --> 00:49:43,714
THIS ONE DEATH

841
00:49:43,714 --> 00:49:47,651
WILL PROVIDE ME WITH AN ARMY
OF INVINCIBLE WARRIORS.

842
00:49:47,651 --> 00:49:49,887
- HE’S GOT A GOITER.
- MILLIONS OF LOST SOULS

843
00:49:49,887 --> 00:49:51,856
- STOP SPITTING.
- TRAPPED DEEP BENEATH THE EARTH

844
00:49:51,856 --> 00:49:55,926
WILL RISE FROM THEIR GRAVE
AND SIDE WITH ME!

845
00:49:55,926 --> 00:49:57,862
YOU USE TOO MUCH MOOSE.

846
00:49:57,862 --> 00:50:00,731
I SHALL RULE THE WORLD.

847
00:50:00,731 --> 00:50:02,800
TAKE HIM OUT TO THE WOODS
AND KILL HIM.

848
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:05,436
AND TAKE AWAY HIS BLOW COMB.

849
00:50:06,871 --> 00:50:08,772
SPREAD OUT. FIND THE BOY.

850
00:50:08,772 --> 00:50:11,742
SIR, UM, SHOULD WE PICK A PLACE
TO MEET BACK, OR...

851
00:50:11,742 --> 00:50:14,545
I GUESS NOT THEN. OKAY.

852
00:50:14,545 --> 00:50:17,548
YUP.

853
00:50:23,120 --> 00:50:26,557
THE ANCIENT CIVILIZATION’S
TOILET KEEPS RUNNING.

854
00:50:29,126 --> 00:50:31,896
A TREASURY
OF SERGIO ARAGONES SKETCHES.

855
00:50:31,896 --> 00:50:33,497
COOL.

856
00:50:39,103 --> 00:50:43,173
OH, I WILL HAVE THIS PAINTED
ON THE SIDE OF MY VAN SOMEDAY.

857
00:50:46,877 --> 00:50:49,013
HELLO?

858
00:50:49,013 --> 00:50:51,382
YOU, UH, GOT A PREFERENCE
ABOUT WHERE YOU’D LIKE US

859
00:50:51,382 --> 00:50:53,083
TO KILL YOU, EH?

860
00:50:56,453 --> 00:50:58,055
NOW, TOMORROW’S CASUAL DAY.

861
00:50:58,055 --> 00:51:00,324
I THINK I’M GOING TO WEAR
A YELLOW T-SHIRT.

862
00:51:04,128 --> 00:51:06,730
AH, I’VE ESCAPED-- AAH!

863
00:51:09,733 --> 00:51:11,802
CRIPES, HE ROLLED
OUT OF BOUNDS.

864
00:51:16,941 --> 00:51:18,876
WHAT IS THIS OBSESSION
WITH NOT SHOWING US

865
00:51:18,876 --> 00:51:20,244
WHO’S GETTING INTO
WHAT TRUCK?

866
00:51:20,244 --> 00:51:21,779
I DON’T KNOW.

867
00:51:26,417 --> 00:51:27,885
HE’S GOT A FUNNY TAN LINE.

868
00:51:27,885 --> 00:51:29,453
YEAH.

869
00:51:34,725 --> 00:51:39,296
OH, NO, THEY’VE GOT A CHEVY.
THEY’RE SO DEPENDABLE!

870
00:51:39,296 --> 00:51:43,000
QUICK, CLIMB A TREE.
TRUCKS CAN’T CLIMB TREES.

871
00:51:47,404 --> 00:51:48,872
OOH, YOU KNOW IF YOU HIT
A ROWSDOWER,

872
00:51:48,872 --> 00:51:50,341
YOU GET TO KEEP IT.

873
00:51:50,341 --> 00:51:54,345
THE MEAT’S A BIT GAMEY,
BUT IT’S GOOD FOR SAUSAGE.

874
00:51:54,345 --> 00:51:57,548
[TIRES SQUEALING]

875
00:51:57,548 --> 00:52:00,451
UH, I’M OKAY.
WANT TO TRY AGAIN?

876
00:52:02,386 --> 00:52:03,754
GRASS STAINS.

877
00:52:03,754 --> 00:52:06,190
WHEN YOU’VE GOT CULTS,
YOU’VE GOT TO HAVE TIDE.

878
00:52:08,559 --> 00:52:09,860
DEAR COUNSELOR TROY,

879
00:52:09,860 --> 00:52:12,596
I WAITED AT DENNY’S,
BUT YOU DIDN’T MEET ME.

880
00:52:15,366 --> 00:52:16,834
DEAR AGENT SCULLY,

881
00:52:16,834 --> 00:52:20,504
DID NOT APPRECIATE
YOUR LAWYER’S TONE.

882
00:52:25,009 --> 00:52:26,677
AND SO, IT IS
WITH A HEAVY HEART

883
00:52:26,677 --> 00:52:30,347
THAT I MUST RESIGN
FROM CHESS CLUB.

884
00:52:30,347 --> 00:52:32,583
WHERE OUR TOKEN CROSSES...

885
00:52:34,818 --> 00:52:37,588
THE CITY IS LOCATED.

886
00:52:37,588 --> 00:52:39,056
HMM?

887
00:52:39,056 --> 00:52:41,025
MAN, I SOLVED MYST
IN TEN MINUTES,

888
00:52:41,025 --> 00:52:42,893
WHY CAN’T I DO THIS?

889
00:52:45,763 --> 00:52:49,266
THIS IS A PASSIVE SENTENCE,
I BETTER ALERT MY ENGLISH CLUB.

890
00:52:49,266 --> 00:52:52,336
BACK! BACK,
YOU SILVERFISH, BACK!

891
00:52:55,072 --> 00:52:58,208
[GRUNTS]

892
00:53:04,848 --> 00:53:07,785
I CAN SEE WHY QUEBEC WANTS
TO BE SEPARATE FROM ALL THIS.

893
00:53:07,785 --> 00:53:09,353
MM-HMM.

894
00:53:12,689 --> 00:53:16,193
HE WAS RAISED
BY A FAMILY OF MOLES.

895
00:53:21,598 --> 00:53:25,002
WAIT, I HAVE AN APPOINTMENT
TO GET BEAT UP.

896
00:53:29,773 --> 00:53:31,241
LOOK LIKE A TWIG.

897
00:53:31,241 --> 00:53:33,744
OH, THAT SHOULDN’T BE HARD.

898
00:53:35,979 --> 00:53:38,949
SIR, YOU HAVE A HOLE
IN YOUR SHOE. OOPS! SSH.

899
00:53:44,021 --> 00:53:46,924
HE’S BUILT LIKE
A WOMAN PHY-ED TEACHER.

900
00:53:49,426 --> 00:53:52,463
MY SHIRT IS CHARCOAL,
THAT’S BASICALLY BLACK.

901
00:53:54,531 --> 00:53:57,568
THIS IS JUST LIKE WHEN THEY
BURY ME EVERY WEEK AT SCHOOL.

902
00:53:57,568 --> 00:53:59,670
AND GIVE ME PINK BELLY,
AND HANG ME FROM THE GOAL POST,

903
00:53:59,670 --> 00:54:01,705
AND SHAVE MY HEAD,
AND MAGIC MARKER MY WEENIE,

904
00:54:01,705 --> 00:54:03,974
AND STUFF ME IN MY LOCKER.

905
00:54:10,147 --> 00:54:13,150
[MONKEY NOISES]

906
00:54:13,150 --> 00:54:14,651
[GUNSHOT]

907
00:54:14,651 --> 00:54:18,755
MUST SLIP BACK
AND SELL CANDY BARS FOR BAND.

908
00:54:24,428 --> 00:54:27,731
UH, I’M JUST A BUSH.
YOU MAY WANT TO PAN OFF ME.

909
00:54:31,034 --> 00:54:35,072
WHAT THE-- HEY,
I HAD A BEAD ON A GOOD EH.

910
00:54:35,072 --> 00:54:38,342
EH, EH, EH...

911
00:54:42,846 --> 00:54:45,749
[MACHINE GUN FIRE]
[HUMMING OLYMPIC THEME]

912
00:54:45,749 --> 00:54:49,086
GILLES, NO!

913
00:54:49,086 --> 00:54:51,121
NOT ETIENNE!

914
00:54:54,958 --> 00:54:56,260
I’M IN NO PARTICULAR HURRY.

915
00:54:56,260 --> 00:54:59,029
THE CULT’S GOT THEIR SCHEDULE,
I GOT MINE.

916
00:55:05,335 --> 00:55:07,171
HEY, ARE THEY AFTER ME?

917
00:55:10,073 --> 00:55:13,310
 ZUT ALORS!
 JE SUIS MORT!

918
00:55:16,914 --> 00:55:19,816
- HEY, BOYS IN THE HOODS!
- AH, MAN.

919
00:55:19,816 --> 00:55:22,753
DROP DEAD.

920
00:55:22,753 --> 00:55:26,089
MIKE, WOULD YOU SAY THESE GUYS
ARE IN A HEAVILY FORESTED AREA?

921
00:55:26,089 --> 00:55:28,058
UH, YEAH SURE.

922
00:55:28,058 --> 00:55:29,960
WOULD YOU CALL THESE
THE DEEP WOODS?

923
00:55:29,960 --> 00:55:31,929
YEAH.

924
00:55:31,929 --> 00:55:33,997
BECAUSE-- BECAUSE WHEN
YOU’RE IN THE WOODS,

925
00:55:33,997 --> 00:55:37,034
YOU CAN’T BEAT THE RELIABLE,
REASONABLY PRICED

926
00:55:37,034 --> 00:55:41,038
MOSQUITO REPELLANT "OFF."

927
00:55:41,038 --> 00:55:43,841
[LAUGHS]
MAN, YOU NEVER EVEN
SAW THAT COMING, DID YOU?

928
00:55:48,512 --> 00:55:51,048
- WAIT, IT’S ME!
- I KNOW.

929
00:55:53,517 --> 00:55:55,452
AH, THEY’RE ELOPING.

930
00:56:00,624 --> 00:56:02,559
UGH, THIS IS JUST LIKE

931
00:56:02,559 --> 00:56:06,096
WHEN I ALMOST MISSED
MY "TEENS ENCOUNTER CHRIST" BUS.

932
00:56:10,234 --> 00:56:11,501
COME ON,
IT WAS LIKE 30 YARDS.

933
00:56:15,038 --> 00:56:17,541
YEAH, MY HAIR’S A MESS.
SO WHAT?

934
00:56:19,142 --> 00:56:20,777
YOU WERE ONE OF THEM?

935
00:56:20,777 --> 00:56:24,047
AN UNCOOKED
BRATWURST WITH HAIR.

936
00:56:24,047 --> 00:56:25,349
[PANTING]

937
00:56:25,349 --> 00:56:26,516
I WAS.

938
00:56:26,516 --> 00:56:29,219
I WAS ONLY PART-TIME,
AND I GOT LAID OFF.

939
00:56:29,219 --> 00:56:31,788
YEARS AGO.

940
00:56:31,788 --> 00:56:33,190
WHY?

941
00:56:33,190 --> 00:56:35,726
LET ME DIE FIRST,
THEN I’LL TELL YOU.

942
00:56:37,294 --> 00:56:39,429
IT STARTED
WITH THE NIGHTMARES.

943
00:56:39,429 --> 00:56:41,298
[RHYTHMIC HUMMING]

944
00:56:41,298 --> 00:56:43,600
THEN DRUMS.

945
00:56:43,600 --> 00:56:45,402
THEY WERE CALLING ME.

946
00:56:45,402 --> 00:56:47,638
WOW, NOBODY EVER CALLS ME.

947
00:56:47,638 --> 00:56:49,773
IT WAS SATORIS,
HE STARTED IT ALL.

948
00:56:49,773 --> 00:56:51,141
HOW?

949
00:56:51,141 --> 00:56:54,511
HE’S PSYCHOTIC.

950
00:56:54,511 --> 00:56:57,314
TOO MANY PEOPLE
UNDERESTIMATED HIM,
AND DIED MYSTERIOUSLY.

951
00:56:59,416 --> 00:57:03,453
HOLD ON, I’M HAVING A SERIES
OF ELABORATE HEART-ATTACKS.

952
00:57:03,453 --> 00:57:05,389
IS THAT HOW
MY FATHER WAS KILLED?

953
00:57:05,389 --> 00:57:07,457
I’M NOT TELLING.

954
00:57:10,360 --> 00:57:11,495
I DON’T KNOW.

955
00:57:11,495 --> 00:57:15,399
UGH, NOW IT’S
TURNED INTO A STROKE!

956
00:57:15,399 --> 00:57:18,502
SATORIS FOUND OUT
I WAS ONLY A HALF-BLOOD.

957
00:57:18,502 --> 00:57:20,704
SOON AFTER, HE THREW ME OUT.

958
00:57:20,704 --> 00:57:22,706
I-- SSH.

959
00:57:22,706 --> 00:57:25,642
OH, IT’S JUST A JACKALOPE.

960
00:57:25,642 --> 00:57:28,645
LET’S GET OUT OF HERE.
THIS WAY.

961
00:57:28,645 --> 00:57:32,082
HMM, THAT’S A LITTLE TOO MUCH
DéCOLLETAGE FOR ME.

962
00:57:34,251 --> 00:57:37,321
AH, ANY GIVEN WEEKEND
IN CANADA.

963
00:57:39,856 --> 00:57:43,226
SIDES OF HIS HEART
ARE BLOWING OUT LIKE OLD TIRES.

964
00:57:43,226 --> 00:57:47,464
[TIRE POPPING SOUNDS]

965
00:57:47,464 --> 00:57:49,599
[PANTING]

966
00:57:53,570 --> 00:57:57,507
ROWSDOWER!

967
00:57:57,507 --> 00:58:00,243
[PANTING]

968
00:58:00,243 --> 00:58:02,913
THIS IS FUN!

969
00:58:05,749 --> 00:58:09,353
THEY’VE STUMBLED UPON
GEDDY LEE’S BIRTHPLACE.

970
00:58:09,353 --> 00:58:10,954
OKAY.

971
00:58:10,954 --> 00:58:12,289
I GUESS WE’VE HAD IT.

972
00:58:12,289 --> 00:58:15,992
I PROBABLY ONLY HAD ABOUT
THREE MORE MONTHS ANYWAY.

973
00:58:15,992 --> 00:58:17,994
NOT YET.

974
00:58:17,994 --> 00:58:20,530
IT’S THE WIZARD OF ID BIATHLON

975
00:58:24,568 --> 00:58:28,405
HEY IT LOOKS LIKE
THEIR TIN ROOF RUSTED.

976
00:58:32,075 --> 00:58:35,011
ALL RIGHT, ABRAHAM LINCOLN,
STOP WRITING ON THAT DAMN SHOVEL

977
00:58:35,011 --> 00:58:37,013
AND COME OUT
WITH YOUR HANDS UP.

978
00:58:45,422 --> 00:58:46,790
OH, THIS IS NO BIG DEAL.

979
00:58:46,790 --> 00:58:51,395
IT’S HOW I GET THROUGH
EVERY SCHOOL DAY.

980
00:58:51,395 --> 00:58:55,232
WINNIPEG CONFIDENTIAL.

981
00:58:55,232 --> 00:58:57,567
I SHOULD TELL YOU THAT I WHEEZE
LOUDLY WHEN I’M SCARED.

982
00:58:57,567 --> 00:59:01,071
[WHEEZING]

983
00:59:01,071 --> 00:59:05,575
UH, GUILLAUME, THIS IS MY PLACE.
DO YOU MIND?

984
00:59:05,575 --> 00:59:07,778
MAN, THEY’RE BOUND
TO SMELL ME.

985
00:59:10,614 --> 00:59:11,948
[GASPS]

986
00:59:11,948 --> 00:59:13,817
D’OH.

987
00:59:13,817 --> 00:59:16,119
 A MERDE. MON PIED!

988
00:59:18,455 --> 00:59:20,924
DAMN, BROKE A HEEL.

989
00:59:23,627 --> 00:59:25,662
GUY UPSTAIRS
HAD BAD ENURESIS.

990
00:59:25,662 --> 00:59:29,232
I’LL SAY.

991
00:59:29,232 --> 00:59:31,601
UGH, I’VE BEEN PULLING ZIOX
DOUBLE SHIFTS ALL WEEK.

992
00:59:31,601 --> 00:59:35,272
IT’S KILLING ME.

993
00:59:35,272 --> 00:59:39,776
UGH, I HAVEN’T BEEN THIS TENSE
SINCE MOCK U.N.

994
00:59:42,345 --> 00:59:45,482
IS IT POSSIBLE TO TRASH
A GARBAGE HOUSE.

995
00:59:48,852 --> 00:59:51,888
THIS WAS GRANDMA’S
HUNTING SHACK.

996
00:59:51,888 --> 00:59:53,557
LISTEN.

997
00:59:53,557 --> 00:59:54,891
[CROW CAWING]

998
00:59:54,891 --> 00:59:57,093
- IT’S HECKLE!
- NO, IT’S CLEARLY JECKLE.

999
00:59:57,093 --> 01:00:00,464
OH, YOU’RE RIGHT.

1000
01:00:00,464 --> 01:00:02,199
HMM, THEY SHOT
A PAIR OF SNOWSHOES,

1001
01:00:02,199 --> 01:00:04,100
AND HAD THEM STUFFED
AND MOUNTED.

1002
01:00:07,237 --> 01:00:10,874
- FOOD!
- YEAH, NO BEER THOUGH.

1003
01:00:13,276 --> 01:00:15,812
MORE FOOD!

1004
01:00:19,349 --> 01:00:21,618
WHAT THE HELL
ARE YOU DOING HERE?

1005
01:00:21,618 --> 01:00:24,154
WE WERE EATING YOUR FOOD.

1006
01:00:27,157 --> 01:00:28,592
AGAINST THE WALL.

1007
01:00:28,592 --> 01:00:32,162
IT’S GORDON LIGHTFOOT
AT HOME.

1008
01:00:32,162 --> 01:00:35,065
CURSED CULT LEADER
SEND YOU HERES BY ME?

1009
01:00:35,065 --> 01:00:36,600
[IMITATING ACCENT]
YOU KNOW HIM?

1010
01:00:36,600 --> 01:00:41,071
GET ’EM UP!
GET ’EM UP!

1011
01:00:41,071 --> 01:00:43,173
SPLATTER YOUR BRAINS
ALL OVER THIS PLACE.

1012
01:00:43,173 --> 01:00:46,576
NO, AS A MATTER OF FACT,
WE JUST ESCAPED FROM HIM.

1013
01:00:46,576 --> 01:00:50,447
THEN WHAT’S THAT THERE MARK
DOING ON YOUR SHOULDER THERE?

1014
01:00:50,447 --> 01:00:53,316
IT’S A LONG STORY.
McGREGGOR, TELL HIM.

1015
01:00:53,316 --> 01:00:55,285
- McGREGGOR?
- GREGGOR!

1016
01:00:55,285 --> 01:00:57,053
- TROY McGREGGOR?
- IT MUST HURT.

1017
01:00:57,053 --> 01:00:59,389
THOMAS’ SON?

1018
01:00:59,389 --> 01:01:01,925
YEAH.

1019
01:01:01,925 --> 01:01:06,263
- DID YOU KNOW HIM?
- KNOW HIM? HE WAS DELICIOUS!

1020
01:01:06,263 --> 01:01:08,198
♪♪

1021
01:01:13,236 --> 01:01:15,872
MY NAME’S PIPPER.
MIKE PIPPER.

1022
01:01:15,872 --> 01:01:18,808
YOUR DAD AND ME WERE PARTNERS
IN ARCHAEOLOGY.

1023
01:01:18,808 --> 01:01:20,544
PIPPER PARTNER.

1024
01:01:20,544 --> 01:01:22,612
MANY DIGS WE DID TOGETHER.

1025
01:01:22,612 --> 01:01:24,881
[GRUNTS]
PIPPER DIGS.

1026
01:01:24,881 --> 01:01:26,550
GOOD MAN HE WAS, YOUR DAD.

1027
01:01:26,550 --> 01:01:29,920
[LAUGHS]
ALWAYS LAUGHING.

1028
01:01:29,920 --> 01:01:31,187
STUBBORN THOUGH.

1029
01:01:31,187 --> 01:01:33,790
ANOTHER HELPING
OF FILTH FOR YOU?

1030
01:01:38,862 --> 01:01:40,230
WHAT HAPPENED TO HIM?

1031
01:01:40,230 --> 01:01:42,499
I JERKED HIM.

1032
01:01:42,499 --> 01:01:45,635
- I’LL TELL YOU.
- OKAY.

1033
01:01:45,635 --> 01:01:49,005
THE LAST YEAR
YOUR FATHER AND I WERE TOGETHER,

1034
01:01:49,005 --> 01:01:50,307
[GRUNTS]

1035
01:01:50,307 --> 01:01:53,677
WE WAS SEARCHING
FOR A LOST CIVILIZATION.

1036
01:01:53,677 --> 01:01:55,045
ZIOX CIVILIZATION?

1037
01:01:55,045 --> 01:01:57,013
- THAT’S RIGHT.
- YEAH.

1038
01:01:57,013 --> 01:01:59,716
WE MADE CALCULATIONS
AS TO WHERE THE REMAINS

1039
01:01:59,716 --> 01:02:02,519
OF THEIR CITY
MIGHT BE LOCATED.

1040
01:02:02,519 --> 01:02:04,888
THAT’S WHERE
WE RAN INTO SATORIS’ CULT.

1041
01:02:04,888 --> 01:02:07,924
BY THE WAY,
I HATES THAT RABBIT.

1042
01:02:07,924 --> 01:02:10,961
THEY WANTED OUR INFORMATION.

1043
01:02:10,961 --> 01:02:14,598
THOMAS WAS TOO STUBBORN,
SO THEY KILLED HIM.

1044
01:02:14,598 --> 01:02:16,199
POOR OLD THOMAS.

1045
01:02:16,199 --> 01:02:18,501
COULD I DRINK HIM? NO.

1046
01:02:18,501 --> 01:02:20,804
FLED HERE.

1047
01:02:20,804 --> 01:02:23,139
THIS WAS ONE OF
OUR BASE CAMPS.

1048
01:02:23,139 --> 01:02:25,809
LIVED HERE EVER SINCE.

1049
01:02:25,809 --> 01:02:28,445
WHAT DO YOU KNOW
ABOUT SATORIS?

1050
01:02:28,445 --> 01:02:31,881
TO UNDERSTAND HIM,
YOU MUST KNOW ABOUT THE ZIOX.

1051
01:02:31,881 --> 01:02:33,984
ZIOX,
NOW WITH LAPITITHAMINE.

1052
01:02:33,984 --> 01:02:37,387
NOW, THOUSANDS OF YEARS AGO,
LONG BEFORE THE INDIANS,

1053
01:02:37,387 --> 01:02:39,789
- YEAH.
- THIS LAND WAS INHABITED
BY THE ZIOX.

1054
01:02:39,789 --> 01:02:40,924
NO IT WASN’T.

1055
01:02:40,924 --> 01:02:43,026
THEY’RE A HIGHLY
INTELLIGENT RACE.

1056
01:02:43,026 --> 01:02:47,564
FAR ADVANCED IN SCIENCE
AND ARCHITECTURE AND LITERATURE.

1057
01:02:47,564 --> 01:02:48,832
NO THEY WEREN’T.

1058
01:02:48,832 --> 01:02:50,667
- THEY BUILT A HUGE CITY.
- NO THEY DIDN’T.

1059
01:02:50,667 --> 01:02:53,169
FAR GRANDER THAN ANYTHING
THE OLD ROMANS OR THE EGYPTIANS

1060
01:02:53,169 --> 01:02:55,505
HAD EVER KNOWN.

1061
01:02:55,505 --> 01:02:58,441
THE BUILDINGS WERE COVERED
IN GOLD AND SILVER.

1062
01:02:58,441 --> 01:02:59,776
MATTED HAIR.

1063
01:02:59,776 --> 01:03:02,045
IN THE CENTER,
THEY BUILT A TEMPLE

1064
01:03:02,045 --> 01:03:04,147
TO PRAISE THEIR GOD.

1065
01:03:04,147 --> 01:03:07,017
THEN THEY PUT A BOTTLE BRUSH
DOWN MY THROAT.

1066
01:03:07,017 --> 01:03:08,685
IT’S ALL GONE NOW.

1067
01:03:08,685 --> 01:03:11,588
ERASED FROM EXISTENCE.

1068
01:03:11,588 --> 01:03:13,323
- HOW?
- NO, NO, DON’T ENCOURAGE HIM!

1069
01:03:13,323 --> 01:03:16,559
- GEE WHIZ.
- IT IS A MYSTERY.

1070
01:03:16,559 --> 01:03:18,228
AS THE LEGEND GOES,

1071
01:03:18,228 --> 01:03:20,063
THERE WAS A PERIOD
OF GREAT WEALTH.

1072
01:03:20,063 --> 01:03:23,133
BROUGHT DISCONTENTMENT
TO THE PEOPLE.

1073
01:03:23,133 --> 01:03:27,270
- PEOPLE BEGAN TO FEAR.
- MM. GOOD DOPE.

1074
01:03:27,270 --> 01:03:29,305
- FEAR BROUGHT SUPERSTITION.
- YEAH.

1075
01:03:29,305 --> 01:03:31,708
SO THEY BUILT AN IDOL.

1076
01:03:31,708 --> 01:03:35,278
WELL, THEIR GOD CURSED THEM
AND FLOODED THE LAND

1077
01:03:35,278 --> 01:03:38,048
WITH A RAINSTORM
THAT LAST A FULL MONTH.

1078
01:03:38,048 --> 01:03:39,616
THEIR BASEMENTS GOT WET.

1079
01:03:39,616 --> 01:03:41,484
SOIL BECAME SO SOFT,

1080
01:03:41,484 --> 01:03:43,953
CITY SANK
INTO A HUGE QUAGMIRE.

1081
01:03:43,953 --> 01:03:46,222
WAIT, I’M A HUGE QUAGMIRE.

1082
01:03:46,222 --> 01:03:49,926
SURVIVORS WERE DOOMED
TO ROAM THE EARTH.

1083
01:03:49,926 --> 01:03:53,163
THAT’S-- THIS CULT IS ALL
THAT’S LEFT OF THEM.

1084
01:03:53,163 --> 01:03:55,598
HEY, WHAT’S THIS A PILE OF?
OH, CRAP. THAT’S RIGHT.

1085
01:03:55,598 --> 01:03:57,500
SATORIS BELIEVE IN THE IDOL.

1086
01:03:57,500 --> 01:03:59,803
HE THINKS THAT BY SACRIFICING
SOMEONE TO IT,

1087
01:03:59,803 --> 01:04:01,604
IT’LL PROVIDE HIM WITH AN
INVINCIBLE ARMY

1088
01:04:01,604 --> 01:04:03,073
THAT CAN CONQUER THE WORLD.

1089
01:04:03,073 --> 01:04:05,608
EXCEPT THAT IF
THE IDOL’S EVER DESTROYED,

1090
01:04:05,608 --> 01:04:08,778
THE OLD CITY WILL RETURN
TO ITS FORMER GLORY.

1091
01:04:08,778 --> 01:04:11,548
IT’S A SYMBOL OF GOOD.

1092
01:04:11,548 --> 01:04:14,851
MEAN THE END
TO SATORIS’ POWER.

1093
01:04:14,851 --> 01:04:18,354
UH, THESE ARE ALL LEGENDS,
OF COURSE.

1094
01:04:18,354 --> 01:04:21,324
- WAIT A MINUTE.
- I HAVE A GAG IN MY POCKET.

1095
01:04:23,460 --> 01:04:25,295
- LOOK.
- OOH, WHAT IS THAT?

1096
01:04:25,295 --> 01:04:27,163
GIVE ME THAT, VARMINT.

1097
01:04:30,100 --> 01:04:31,501
YOUR FATHER MADE THIS.

1098
01:04:31,501 --> 01:04:32,969
DIDN’T DO A VERY GOOD JOB.

1099
01:04:32,969 --> 01:04:35,238
WE FOUND THE ORIGINAL
IN A SECRET CHAMBER

1100
01:04:35,238 --> 01:04:36,239
NOT FAR FROM HERE.

1101
01:04:36,239 --> 01:04:37,407
WE KNOW.

1102
01:04:37,407 --> 01:04:38,742
I TRANSLATED THE SENTENCE

1103
01:04:38,742 --> 01:04:41,811
WITH THE HELP
OF MY FATHER’S NOTES.

1104
01:04:41,811 --> 01:04:44,114
"WHERE OUR TOKEN CROSSES,

1105
01:04:44,114 --> 01:04:46,883
THE CITY IS LOCATED."

1106
01:04:46,883 --> 01:04:48,218
WHAT DOES IT MEAN?

1107
01:04:48,218 --> 01:04:51,121
IT MEANS "OOH, I’M GONNA HOG-TIE
THAT VARMINT."

1108
01:04:57,460 --> 01:05:01,664
[JABBERING]

1109
01:05:01,664 --> 01:05:04,734
HE’S PLAYING
CONNECT THE GODS.

1110
01:05:04,734 --> 01:05:07,303
♪ COME AND SIT BY MY SIDE
IF YOU LOVE ME ♪

1111
01:05:07,303 --> 01:05:10,573
♪ DO NOT HASTEN
TO BID ME ADIEU, OOH ♪

1112
01:05:16,713 --> 01:05:20,316
OOH, I NEEDS AN ERASER!

1113
01:05:20,316 --> 01:05:22,385
HERE’S THE PLAN,
MY ARMY OF TRAINED RATS

1114
01:05:22,385 --> 01:05:23,486
WILL LEAD THE CHARGE,

1115
01:05:23,486 --> 01:05:26,589
AND MY SCABIES
WILL PROTECT OUR FLANK.

1116
01:05:30,727 --> 01:05:34,197
WELL...

1117
01:05:34,197 --> 01:05:36,566
- PIPPER CAM.
- IT’S A SYMBOL!

1118
01:05:36,566 --> 01:05:38,468
EMPEROR HAILE SELASSIE.

1119
01:05:38,468 --> 01:05:42,806
WHERE THE LINES CROSS IS
THE EXACT LOCATION OF THE CITY.

1120
01:05:42,806 --> 01:05:46,075
- AND THE IDOL?
- OOH! I HATES THOSE QUESTIONS.

1121
01:05:46,075 --> 01:05:48,011
I KNOW WHAT YOU’RE THINKING.

1122
01:05:48,011 --> 01:05:51,181
ME AND THOMAS SEARCHED
AND FOUND NOTHING.

1123
01:05:51,181 --> 01:05:52,816
THE IDOL’S A LEGEND.

1124
01:05:52,816 --> 01:05:54,384
I HATES LEGENDS.

1125
01:05:54,384 --> 01:05:57,854
[LAUGHTER]

1126
01:05:57,854 --> 01:05:59,222
ALL RIGHT.

1127
01:05:59,222 --> 01:06:01,191
IT’S BEEN DEAD AND GONE
FOR MORE THAN 1,000 YEARS.

1128
01:06:01,191 --> 01:06:02,792
BUT THE CULT IS ALIVE.

1129
01:06:02,792 --> 01:06:05,161
- OOH!
- YEAH, THE CULT’S ALIVE.

1130
01:06:05,161 --> 01:06:07,697
BUT ITS BELIEFS
ARE BASED ON LEGENDS.

1131
01:06:07,697 --> 01:06:10,466
IN TIME, THE CULT MEMBERS
WILL FIND OUT OF THEMSELVES.

1132
01:06:10,466 --> 01:06:12,602
AND THE CULT
WILL GRADUALLY BE DISSOLVED.

1133
01:06:12,602 --> 01:06:15,305
AND HOW MANY LIVES
WILL THEY CLAIM
BEFORE THIS HAPPENS?

1134
01:06:15,305 --> 01:06:18,308
GO HOME.
FORGET ABOUT THE CULT.

1135
01:06:18,308 --> 01:06:20,710
DON’T LET IT DESTROY
YOUR LIFE TOO.

1136
01:06:20,710 --> 01:06:21,811
IT ALREADY HAS.

1137
01:06:21,811 --> 01:06:24,948
LOOK AT MY HAIR.

1138
01:06:24,948 --> 01:06:28,985
WAIT! I WAS GOING TO SING
SOMETHING FROM BONE MACHINE.

1139
01:06:31,421 --> 01:06:35,859
IF IT’S ANY CONSOLATION,
I HATES THAT RABBIT TOO.

1140
01:06:35,859 --> 01:06:39,062
WELL, WHO’S UP
FOR A MOOSE-LIP OMELET?

1141
01:06:41,598 --> 01:06:43,266
DON’T TRUST THAT MAN.

1142
01:06:43,266 --> 01:06:46,569
I REMEMBER HIM.

1143
01:06:46,569 --> 01:06:49,739
HE WAS WITH SATORIS THE NIGHT
YOUR FATHER WAS KILLED.

1144
01:06:49,739 --> 01:06:52,242
THERE’S THE DOOR.
I CAN JUST LEAVE.

1145
01:06:56,112 --> 01:06:57,213
YOU DON’T MEAN THAT--

1146
01:06:57,213 --> 01:06:58,581
KILLED YOUR FATHER?

1147
01:06:58,581 --> 01:07:01,851
SOUNDS FUN, BUT I’M BUSY.

1148
01:07:01,851 --> 01:07:04,354
I DON’T KNOW.

1149
01:07:06,656 --> 01:07:09,659
WELL, HOW ABOUT
A GAME OF BALDERDASH?

1150
01:07:09,659 --> 01:07:12,962
OOH, FRESH TOWELS
IN THE GUEST ROOM.

1151
01:07:25,541 --> 01:07:28,745
[HUMMING]
NOTHING? ABSOLUTELY NOTHING?

1152
01:07:28,745 --> 01:07:29,879
NOPE, NOPE. SORRY, CROW.

1153
01:07:29,879 --> 01:07:31,147
BUT FROM EVERYTHING
I’VE READ HERE,

1154
01:07:31,147 --> 01:07:32,782
THERE’S NOTHING WE CAN DO
ABOUT HOCKEY HAIR.

1155
01:07:32,782 --> 01:07:34,817
WE JUST HAVE TO GET
PLENTY OF REST AND HOCKEY,

1156
01:07:34,817 --> 01:07:35,885
AND LET IT
TAKE CARE OF ITSELF.

1157
01:07:35,885 --> 01:07:36,886
ALL RIGHT.

1158
01:07:36,886 --> 01:07:38,621
[TOGETHER]
WHOA, MIKE! AAH! SHEESH!

1159
01:07:38,621 --> 01:07:40,857
- HEY, GUYS.
- MIKE, WHAT HAPPENED TO YOU?

1160
01:07:40,857 --> 01:07:43,359
OH, I’M JUST SEEING
WHAT IT’S LIKE TO SMOKE A PIPE.

1161
01:07:43,359 --> 01:07:44,827
NO, NO, NO, IT’S YOUR HAIR.

1162
01:07:44,827 --> 01:07:47,964
IT’S LIKE, UH, IT’S...
LOOK.

1163
01:07:47,964 --> 01:07:50,867
AAH! WHOA! HOLY COW.

1164
01:07:50,867 --> 01:07:52,235
DON’T PANIC, NOW, MIKE.

1165
01:07:52,235 --> 01:07:53,436
YOU’VE SIMPLY GOT A CASE

1166
01:07:53,436 --> 01:07:55,438
OF GRIZZLED OLD
PROSPECTOR SYNDROME.

1167
01:07:55,438 --> 01:07:56,673
- WHOA, MAN.
- IT’S NOT SURPRISING.

1168
01:07:56,673 --> 01:07:58,541
IT IS ASSOCIATED
WITH IMMUNITY TO HOCKEY HAIR.

1169
01:07:58,541 --> 01:08:00,810
YEAH, IT MAY NOT EVEN BE
A FULL-BLOWN INFECTION.

1170
01:08:00,810 --> 01:08:03,179
UNLESS YOU’VE BEEN SAYING
"CONSARN IT" A LOT.

1171
01:08:03,179 --> 01:08:05,315
- NOPE, CONSARN IT CAN’T--
- OH!

1172
01:08:05,315 --> 01:08:06,916
- AH, DAGNABBIT!
- OH!

1173
01:08:06,916 --> 01:08:09,619
OH, WELL, FIDDLESTICKS!
LITTLE VARMINTS.

1174
01:08:09,619 --> 01:08:11,487
I GUESS I AM HORNSWOGGLED.

1175
01:08:11,487 --> 01:08:13,523
WELL, WHAT DO YOU RECKON
I SHOULD DO ABOUT IT?

1176
01:08:13,523 --> 01:08:15,391
UH, LET’S SEE...

1177
01:08:15,391 --> 01:08:16,526
NOTHING TO DO, MIKE,

1178
01:08:16,526 --> 01:08:17,794
YOU JUST GOT TO LET IT
RUN ITS COURSE.

1179
01:08:17,794 --> 01:08:19,662
YEAH, YOU’LL WANT
TO PAN FOR GOLD, PROBABLY.

1180
01:08:19,662 --> 01:08:22,231
- YOU’LL PROBABLY BUY A MULE.
- AL RIGHT, WELL...

1181
01:08:22,231 --> 01:08:23,232
I WONDER HOW I PICKED IT UP.

1182
01:08:23,232 --> 01:08:24,467
WELL, LET’S SEE, UM...

1183
01:08:24,467 --> 01:08:26,069
YOU BEEN KISSING
ANY PROSPECTORS?

1184
01:08:26,069 --> 01:08:27,270
- NOPE!
- GOOD, PHEW.

1185
01:08:27,270 --> 01:08:28,371
HOLD ON. WAIT A MINUTE.

1186
01:08:28,371 --> 01:08:30,173
- NO, NO, I HAVEN’T. NO.
- PHEW.

1187
01:08:30,173 --> 01:08:33,242
OH. NO, YOU KNOW WHAT,
THAT WAS A SURLY TRUCK FARMER.

1188
01:08:33,242 --> 01:08:35,678
DARN FINE KISSER THOUGH.

1189
01:08:35,678 --> 01:08:37,480
YOU OLD COOT, HUH?

1190
01:08:37,480 --> 01:08:38,614
UH, WE’LL BE RIGHT BACK.

1191
01:08:38,614 --> 01:08:40,183
YEE-HOO!

1192
01:08:40,183 --> 01:08:42,085
♪♪

1193
01:08:47,190 --> 01:08:49,626
- DAGNABBIT.
- CLEARED RIGHT UP.

1194
01:08:49,626 --> 01:08:53,329
AH, LANGUAGE CAMP
IS SO FAR AWAY.

1195
01:08:59,902 --> 01:09:01,404
I’M TAKING YOU HOME TOMORROW.

1196
01:09:01,404 --> 01:09:04,007
I KNOW MOM AND DAD
WILL JUST LOVE YOU.

1197
01:09:07,377 --> 01:09:08,878
HM?

1198
01:09:08,878 --> 01:09:10,046
TROY.

1199
01:09:10,046 --> 01:09:13,516
MAN, YOU KILL ONE GUY’S DAD.

1200
01:09:18,221 --> 01:09:21,491
I WONDER IF THERE’S BEER
ON THE SUN.

1201
01:09:25,361 --> 01:09:29,999
ROWSDOWER. [SNORING]
ROWSDOWER. [SNORING]

1202
01:09:29,999 --> 01:09:34,003
AH, CRUSTY PANTS,
A FILTHY WALL, GOOD MORNING.

1203
01:09:36,372 --> 01:09:40,143
AH, MAN. THOSE 12 OUNCE CURLS
REALLY TAKE IT OUT OF ME.

1204
01:09:45,048 --> 01:09:47,617
HAVE A DRINK ON ME, TATTOO.

1205
01:09:50,420 --> 01:09:53,022
LEIF GARRETT TODAY.

1206
01:09:56,426 --> 01:10:00,463
WELL, THAT’S ENOUGH
FOR ONE DAY. UGH.

1207
01:10:06,636 --> 01:10:10,807
♪ VAL-DER-EE,
VAL-DER-AH-HA-HA-HA-HA-HA ♪

1208
01:10:14,577 --> 01:10:17,580
MAN, THAT’S
A TERRIBLE GOLF STROKE.

1209
01:10:21,317 --> 01:10:25,254
I’LL PLANT THE ROSES HERE.

1210
01:10:25,254 --> 01:10:28,558
BLEH! AAH! UGH!

1211
01:10:28,558 --> 01:10:31,260
UM, SSS!

1212
01:10:34,464 --> 01:10:37,100
HE’S LAYING ON A BEAR.

1213
01:10:43,840 --> 01:10:46,642
HEY, HE GOT TO SECOND BASE
WITH HIMSELF.

1214
01:10:46,642 --> 01:10:49,011
WHOO!

1215
01:10:49,011 --> 01:10:51,581
WELL, I GOT THAT DONE.

1216
01:10:54,951 --> 01:10:57,086
GOD BLESS MOMMY AND DADDY

1217
01:10:57,086 --> 01:11:01,824
AND GRANDPA
AND ALL MY EVIL HENCHMEN.

1218
01:11:01,824 --> 01:11:05,061
[HUMMING]

1219
01:11:05,061 --> 01:11:08,931
AAH, OH, ANOTHER M.I.

1220
01:11:08,931 --> 01:11:12,235
OH, GREAT.

1221
01:11:16,672 --> 01:11:20,143
HE’S INVOKING
THE POWERS OF BRYAN ADAMS.

1222
01:11:20,143 --> 01:11:24,046
[GRUNTS]

1223
01:11:24,046 --> 01:11:26,449
ONE.

1224
01:11:29,519 --> 01:11:33,122
BONANZA.

1225
01:11:33,122 --> 01:11:34,557
UGH, I’M EXHAUSTED.

1226
01:11:34,557 --> 01:11:39,262
I GOTTA TAKE A NAP
AFTER I’M DONE SLEEPING.

1227
01:11:39,262 --> 01:11:43,332
BLESS MY STICK,
OH, HOLY WILLIE MOSCONI.

1228
01:11:45,635 --> 01:11:49,172
OH, MAN, THAT’S NOT A NOSE,
THAT’S A DUPLEX.

1229
01:11:54,477 --> 01:11:56,813
HEY!

1230
01:11:56,813 --> 01:11:59,949
HEY! AH, THIS’LL TEACH ME.

1231
01:12:02,485 --> 01:12:05,955
HAND ME MY TOP HAT.

1232
01:12:05,955 --> 01:12:09,292
[HUMMING  CHARGE BASEBALL SONG]

1233
01:12:09,292 --> 01:12:11,694
♪ DO-DO-DO-DO DO-DO
CHARGE ♪

1234
01:12:14,530 --> 01:12:18,234
ALL RIGHTY, THE DOCTOR
WILL BE IN TO SEE YOU
IN JUST A MINUTE.

1235
01:12:21,270 --> 01:12:25,675
OOH.

1236
01:12:25,675 --> 01:12:28,144
AW, YOUR S’MORE FELL IN.

1237
01:12:28,144 --> 01:12:30,913
♪ AY-YI-YI
HEY ♪

1238
01:12:30,913 --> 01:12:34,016
♪ AY-YI-YI-YI-YI 
HEY ♪

1239
01:12:34,016 --> 01:12:36,953
♪ AY-YI-YI
HEY ♪

1240
01:12:36,953 --> 01:12:40,389
♪ AY-YI-YI
HEY ♪

1241
01:12:40,389 --> 01:12:43,626
[SINGING CONTINUES]

1242
01:12:50,099 --> 01:12:52,001
VODKA!

1243
01:12:52,001 --> 01:12:54,403
- REALLY?
- NO.

1244
01:12:54,403 --> 01:12:57,240
I GOT KETCHUP ON MY HAND.
[SOBBING]

1245
01:13:01,244 --> 01:13:03,980
WELL, I’M NOT HIRING THESE GUYS
TO DO MY NIPPLE PIERCING.

1246
01:13:03,980 --> 01:13:05,414
AAH!

1247
01:13:05,414 --> 01:13:08,317
OH.

1248
01:13:08,317 --> 01:13:09,785
AAH!

1249
01:13:09,785 --> 01:13:14,223
I FORGOT, THE LIQUOR STORES
CLOSE AT 8:00!

1250
01:13:14,223 --> 01:13:15,725
SORRY.

1251
01:13:15,725 --> 01:13:17,627
TROY?

1252
01:13:17,627 --> 01:13:18,828
TROY.

1253
01:13:18,828 --> 01:13:22,298
NOW MIKE, TECHNICALLY
THAT PAPER IS SMOKIN!

1254
01:13:22,298 --> 01:13:24,800
- NO!
- SORRY.

1255
01:13:28,471 --> 01:13:30,973
KRAMER-DOWER.

1256
01:13:35,411 --> 01:13:36,479
THEY TOOK HIM.

1257
01:13:36,479 --> 01:13:39,181
I GOTTA GO WORK OUT.

1258
01:13:39,181 --> 01:13:40,950
WHY?

1259
01:13:40,950 --> 01:13:43,185
MAN, MY LICE
HAS LEFT MY BEARD.

1260
01:13:43,185 --> 01:13:46,389
WHAT WOULD THEY WANT
WITH THE BOY?

1261
01:13:46,389 --> 01:13:47,757
[HORSE WHINNY]

1262
01:13:47,757 --> 01:13:52,261
HERE, OKAY.

1263
01:13:52,261 --> 01:13:55,665
HAVING A HARD TIME
SADDLING UP THE MISSES TODAY.

1264
01:13:57,733 --> 01:14:02,605
I MADE YOU SOME TRAIL MIX
OUT OF RAT DROPPINGS AND HAIR.

1265
01:14:02,605 --> 01:14:06,742
SHE’S OLD, BUT SHE’S GOT
LOTS OF SPIRIT.

1266
01:14:06,742 --> 01:14:09,745
NOW RIDE, POSTMAN!

1267
01:14:15,351 --> 01:14:16,919
LOOK, I WANT
TO COME WITH YOU.

1268
01:14:16,919 --> 01:14:18,888
NO. IT’S TOO SLOW.

1269
01:14:18,888 --> 01:14:21,257
WHOA. BUT THANKS
FOR EVERYTHING.

1270
01:14:21,257 --> 01:14:22,958
THE FLEAS AND ALL, YOU KNOW.

1271
01:14:22,958 --> 01:14:24,994
HEAD NORTH UNTIL YOU GET
TO THE RIVER.

1272
01:14:24,994 --> 01:14:28,431
FOLLOW IT UPSTREAM.

1273
01:14:28,431 --> 01:14:29,932
[HORSE WHINNIES]

1274
01:14:29,932 --> 01:14:31,801
THE LONE ROWSDOWER.

1275
01:14:31,801 --> 01:14:34,670
[HUMMING THE LONE RANGER THEME]

1276
01:14:34,670 --> 01:14:37,406
OW.

1277
01:14:37,406 --> 01:14:41,744
YEAH, YEAH. I KNOW THE ROUTINE.
NOW, THE DOUBLE JOCK-LOCK.

1278
01:14:43,312 --> 01:14:45,448
OH, GOODIE. YOU’RE GOING TO RIDE
BACK HERE WITH ME!

1279
01:14:45,448 --> 01:14:48,117
YOU GUYS KNOW ANY CAMP SONGS?

1280
01:14:48,117 --> 01:14:50,419
[HUMMING]

1281
01:14:53,856 --> 01:14:55,458
UH, SIR, YOU KNOW,
MAYBE IF YOU GOT RID OF

1282
01:14:55,458 --> 01:14:58,194
THAT HUGE GUNNYSACK
OF GROUND PORK AND--

1283
01:14:58,194 --> 01:15:02,331
OH, THAT’S YOUR BUTT.
I’M SORRY.

1284
01:15:02,331 --> 01:15:06,635
EXCUSE ME A MOMENT.
PLOP, PLOP, PLOP, PLOP. AH.

1285
01:15:08,270 --> 01:15:10,873
MEAT. TA-DA.

1286
01:15:12,842 --> 01:15:16,145
WHY COULDN’T I HAVE BEEN BOUGHT
BY A SEVENTH-GRADE GIRL?

1287
01:15:18,714 --> 01:15:21,684
HANG ON NOW,
IT’S MY TURN TO RIDE YOU.

1288
01:15:24,687 --> 01:15:28,724
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,
MR. ALAN JACKSON.

1289
01:15:31,427 --> 01:15:35,331
ERICH VON STROHEIM
HITCHES ACROSS AMERICA.

1290
01:15:41,170 --> 01:15:45,775
MY GLEE-CLUB
WILL BE LOOKING FOR ME.

1291
01:15:45,775 --> 01:15:50,613
AND FOR YOUR FRIEND ROWSDOWER,
I HOPE HE’S NOT LATE.

1292
01:15:50,613 --> 01:15:53,182
ELSE WE SHALL HAVE TO
START WITHOUT HIM.

1293
01:15:53,182 --> 01:15:54,550
HE’LL BE HERE...

1294
01:15:54,550 --> 01:15:57,219
TO STOP YOU.

1295
01:15:57,219 --> 01:16:00,523
[LAUGHS]
YOU PUSSES MAKE ME LAUGH.

1296
01:16:00,523 --> 01:16:03,325
- I LIKE YOU, TROY.
- EW.

1297
01:16:03,325 --> 01:16:06,328
IT IS A PITY
YOU HAVE TO DIE SO SOON.

1298
01:16:06,328 --> 01:16:08,898
YOU ARE SO MUCH
LIKE YOUR FATHER.

1299
01:16:08,898 --> 01:16:10,266
BRIGHT, STUBBORN...

1300
01:16:10,266 --> 01:16:13,235
WELL, STUBBORN ANYWAY.

1301
01:16:13,235 --> 01:16:15,337
AND IN MY WAY.

1302
01:16:15,337 --> 01:16:17,673
HANG ON, I GOTTA TINKLE.

1303
01:16:17,673 --> 01:16:19,942
WHO KILLED MY FATHER?

1304
01:16:19,942 --> 01:16:22,978
WHY DON’T YOU ASK YOUR FRIEND
WHEN HE ARRIVES?

1305
01:16:22,978 --> 01:16:26,015
HA-HA! THE JOKES ON YOU.
I DON’T HAVE ANY FRIENDS.

1306
01:16:29,652 --> 01:16:31,854
HEY, HOW DID HE GET
GET HIS PANTS CLEAN?

1307
01:16:31,854 --> 01:16:33,422
SAY WHAT YOU WANT
ABOUT THE FILTHY, GRIZZLED GUY,

1308
01:16:33,422 --> 01:16:35,858
HE DOES A GOOD LOAD
OF LAUNDRY.

1309
01:16:37,660 --> 01:16:41,430
[HUMMING, BEATBOXING]

1310
01:16:42,865 --> 01:16:46,368
♪ YOU GOT MUD ON YOUR FACE,
YOU BIG DISGRACE ♪

1311
01:16:46,368 --> 01:16:49,104
♪ SHOVING THOSE SANDWICHES
INTO YOUR FACE ♪

1312
01:16:49,104 --> 01:16:53,209
♪ SINGING WE WILL,
WE WILL ROWSDOWER ♪

1313
01:16:54,410 --> 01:16:55,478
SING IT!

1314
01:16:55,478 --> 01:16:58,314
♪ WE WILL, WE WILL... ♪

1315
01:16:58,314 --> 01:17:00,749
ROWSDOWER.
I GUESS THAT’S OVER.

1316
01:17:02,551 --> 01:17:06,789
HELLO? HAVE YOU SEEN
THE OTHER HOODED THUGS?

1317
01:17:06,789 --> 01:17:09,391
AH, HE SPLASHED AROUND
A LITTLE THUG MUSK

1318
01:17:09,391 --> 01:17:10,693
IN THE AREA TO LURE THEM.

1319
01:17:10,693 --> 01:17:12,094
AH.

1320
01:17:12,094 --> 01:17:13,095
[GUNSHOT]

1321
01:17:13,095 --> 01:17:14,463
OH, I SHOT
RIGHT IN BETWEEN THEM.

1322
01:17:14,463 --> 01:17:16,699
I GOT CONFUSED.

1323
01:17:16,699 --> 01:17:19,902
[HUMMING FIGARO’S ARIA]

1324
01:17:19,902 --> 01:17:22,004
BALANCHINE.

1325
01:17:26,342 --> 01:17:29,678
GERARD, GO THAT WAY.
ROBERT, FOLLOW ME.

1326
01:17:31,847 --> 01:17:34,683
OH, MICHELLE,
THIERRY, HELP ME!

1327
01:17:38,020 --> 01:17:40,489
SMELL MY FINGERS!

1328
01:17:43,025 --> 01:17:46,629
♪♪ [SINGING FIGARO]

1329
01:17:51,500 --> 01:17:56,238
A HORSE!
MY SIX-PACK FOR A HORSE.

1330
01:17:56,238 --> 01:17:57,973
HEY IT TURNS OUT
TO BE MOUNT PINATUBO,

1331
01:17:57,973 --> 01:17:59,408
THEY ALL FALL IN.
THE END. BYE!

1332
01:17:59,408 --> 01:18:01,377
NO, NO, NO,
NO YOU DON’T JUNIOR.

1333
01:18:01,377 --> 01:18:03,512
- GET IN HERE.
- OH.

1334
01:18:09,785 --> 01:18:12,187
[GASPING, CHOKING]

1335
01:18:13,822 --> 01:18:16,625
MY HEART!

1336
01:18:19,562 --> 01:18:21,497
♪♪

1337
01:18:26,502 --> 01:18:31,273
OH, WOW. IT'S
A STUART ANDERSON'S
CATTLE COMPANY CULT.

1338
01:18:31,273 --> 01:18:34,443
- KEEP QUIET.
- MY ROWSDOWER’S COME FOR ME.

1339
01:18:38,814 --> 01:18:42,384
MAMMY! AAH.

1340
01:18:42,384 --> 01:18:46,255
[LAUGHS]
I’M JUST REMEMBERING
A SCENE FROM BIO-DOME.

1341
01:18:48,857 --> 01:18:52,995
CUT YOURSELF LOOSE.
HURRY UP.

1342
01:18:52,995 --> 01:18:54,964
I DROPPED IT.

1343
01:18:58,400 --> 01:19:01,670
MY MEN WILL NOT DISTURB US.

1344
01:19:01,670 --> 01:19:04,540
THEY’RE CLOSING OFF
ALL AVENUES OF ESCAPE.

1345
01:19:04,540 --> 01:19:08,010
DON’T WORRY,
WE WON’T HURT YOU.

1346
01:19:08,010 --> 01:19:10,245
YOU FEAR ME.

1347
01:19:10,245 --> 01:19:13,115
PERHAPS YOU REMEMBER
YOUR LAST DEFEAT.

1348
01:19:13,115 --> 01:19:14,383
AAH!

1349
01:19:14,383 --> 01:19:17,853
HEY, I WASN’T DONE.

1350
01:19:17,853 --> 01:19:20,422
OW!

1351
01:19:20,422 --> 01:19:23,459
WHAT IS THIS, A GRAPPLING HOOK
DUMPING GROUND?

1352
01:19:26,128 --> 01:19:28,364
FIRE BETTER NOT
GET NEAR HIS MOUSSE.

1353
01:19:30,933 --> 01:19:35,537
WHICH IS THE SHARP SIDE?

1354
01:19:35,537 --> 01:19:36,872
HEY, THIS IS IT.

1355
01:19:36,872 --> 01:19:40,542
 THIS IS THE ACTUAL
 CRAZY WORLD OF ARTHUR BROWN.

1356
01:19:40,542 --> 01:19:42,845
UM, I CUT BOTH MY WRISTS.

1357
01:19:42,845 --> 01:19:46,348
SEVEN YEARS AGO, YOU FOUGHT ME
TRYING TO SAVE THOMAS McGREGGOR.

1358
01:19:46,348 --> 01:19:48,284
NOW YOU FIGHT
TO SAVE HIS SON.

1359
01:19:48,284 --> 01:19:49,652
WELL, YOU STARTED IT!

1360
01:19:49,652 --> 01:19:51,020
YOU KILLED HIM,
AND LEFT ME ALIVE

1361
01:19:51,020 --> 01:19:52,855
TO TORMENT
FOR THE REST OF MY LIFE.

1362
01:19:52,855 --> 01:19:54,023
- HM?
- WHAT?

1363
01:19:54,023 --> 01:19:56,291
McGREGGOR REFUSED
TO COOPERATE.

1364
01:19:56,291 --> 01:19:58,193
HE HAD TO DIE.

1365
01:19:58,193 --> 01:20:01,563
YOU WERE GUILTY OF A CRIME
MUCH WORSE THAN HIS.

1366
01:20:01,563 --> 01:20:04,066
YOU BROKE THE SOLE LAW
OF OUR SOCIETY.

1367
01:20:04,066 --> 01:20:06,035
YOU LEFT.

1368
01:20:06,035 --> 01:20:10,539
DEATH WOULD BE TOO MERCIFUL
FOR YOU, ZAP ROWSDOWER.

1369
01:20:10,539 --> 01:20:11,874
ZAP!

1370
01:20:11,874 --> 01:20:15,511
I CHOSE TO LET YOU LIVE
TO BE TORMENTED BY OUR DRUMS

1371
01:20:15,511 --> 01:20:18,414
UNTIL THE END
OF YOUR MISERABLE LIFE.

1372
01:20:18,414 --> 01:20:21,817
AAH!

1373
01:20:21,817 --> 01:20:24,687
UH, I SOMEHOW
SWALLOWED THE KNIFE!

1374
01:20:28,624 --> 01:20:30,993
AND I’M REALLY MAD
THAT YOU NEVER DO THE DISHES

1375
01:20:30,993 --> 01:20:33,128
WHEN IT’S YOUR TURN!

1376
01:20:37,499 --> 01:20:41,503
OH, NICE, ARE THOSE TOTES?
OH, HEY, THEY ARE!

1377
01:20:42,871 --> 01:20:45,340
YOU ARE MINE.

1378
01:20:45,340 --> 01:20:47,409
[GUNSHOT]

1379
01:20:47,409 --> 01:20:50,412
OW. YOU SHOT MY BUTT.
WHAT THE HELL?

1380
01:20:50,412 --> 01:20:54,783
YOU SHOT ME IN THE BUTT!

1381
01:20:54,783 --> 01:20:58,120
YOU WILL BE
THE LAST SACRIFICE.

1382
01:20:58,120 --> 01:21:00,656
THE LAST ONE BETWEEN ME

1383
01:21:00,656 --> 01:21:02,925
AND ULTIMATE POWER
OVER THE EARTH.

1384
01:21:02,925 --> 01:21:04,493
OH, WAIT,
THERE’S ONE GUY AFTER YOU.

1385
01:21:04,493 --> 01:21:06,895
SO YOU’RE--
YOU’RE SECOND TO LAST.

1386
01:21:10,733 --> 01:21:14,002
[GROWLING]

1387
01:21:14,002 --> 01:21:16,305
[YAWNS]

1388
01:21:21,710 --> 01:21:24,179
SO, MIKE, MOST HUMANS,
WHEN YOU SHOOT THEM IN THE BUTT,

1389
01:21:24,179 --> 01:21:25,614
THEY BURST INTO FLAMES?

1390
01:21:25,614 --> 01:21:27,082
WELL, I DON’T KNOW.

1391
01:21:27,082 --> 01:21:29,017
- CAN WE TRY IT? TURN AROUND.
- YEAH, COME ON.

1392
01:21:29,017 --> 01:21:32,121
NO.

1393
01:21:32,121 --> 01:21:33,522
YOU ALL RIGHT, KID?

1394
01:21:33,522 --> 01:21:35,324
WELL, I DON’T HAVE MANY FRIENDS,
GIRLS DON’T LIKE ME,

1395
01:21:35,324 --> 01:21:38,594
AND MY TEACHERS ABSOLUTELY
HATE-- OH, YEAH I’M FINE.

1396
01:21:41,463 --> 01:21:43,031
[THUNDER CLAPS]

1397
01:21:43,031 --> 01:21:47,302
SOMEWHERE, LEE TREVINO
SCURRIES FOR COVER.

1398
01:21:47,302 --> 01:21:50,339
[MOOING]

1399
01:21:53,475 --> 01:21:57,379
THE LEGEND GOES,
IF THE IDOL IS EVER DESTROYED,

1400
01:21:57,379 --> 01:22:00,516
THEN THE CITY WILL RETURN
TO ITS FORMER GLORY.

1401
01:22:00,516 --> 01:22:01,617
UH-HUH.

1402
01:22:01,617 --> 01:22:03,218
IT’S A SYMBOL OF GOOD,

1403
01:22:03,218 --> 01:22:06,155
AND WILL MEAN
THE END OF SATORIS.

1404
01:22:06,155 --> 01:22:08,590
AND REMEMBER, IF THE LADIES
DON’T FIND YOUR HANDSOME,

1405
01:22:08,590 --> 01:22:11,827
AT LEAST YOU SHOULD BE HANDY.

1406
01:22:11,827 --> 01:22:14,329
STAY WITH ME, TROY,
AND I’LL GUIDE YOU IN THE WAYS

1407
01:22:14,329 --> 01:22:17,933
OF ALCOHOL,
CIGARETTES, AND MEAT.

1408
01:22:17,933 --> 01:22:19,301
WELL, IT WAS A PRETTY GOOD CULT,

1409
01:22:19,301 --> 01:22:22,104
BUT HOCKEY’S SEASON’S
STARTING AND ALL.

1410
01:22:24,373 --> 01:22:26,742
OKAY, HOOD-WASHING TIME GUYS.

1411
01:22:26,742 --> 01:22:27,943
LET’S JUST DO THEM
ALL IN ONE LOAD.

1412
01:22:27,943 --> 01:22:30,379
THEY’RE ALL THE SAME COLOR.

1413
01:22:34,316 --> 01:22:37,486
SO, TED, YOU THINK WE’RE GOING
TO GET PAID FOR THIS WEEK?

1414
01:22:42,791 --> 01:22:44,426
[CHUCKLES]

1415
01:22:44,426 --> 01:22:46,995
SOMEBODY REBOOT THE KID.

1416
01:22:50,632 --> 01:22:54,002
THE LOVE CANAL STATE FOREST.

1417
01:22:57,406 --> 01:22:58,740
[CREAKING]

1418
01:22:58,740 --> 01:23:02,711
HEY, I’M IN A SNOWMOBILE CLUB
WITH THAT ONE GUY.

1419
01:23:05,080 --> 01:23:08,817
ROWSDOWER!

1420
01:23:08,817 --> 01:23:11,753
SO THEIR CITY’S
A POP-OUT GREETING CARD.

1421
01:23:14,189 --> 01:23:17,993
THAT’S NOT ACTUALLY A LOST CITY,
IT WAS JUST UNCLAIMED.

1422
01:23:22,598 --> 01:23:24,066
ROWSDOWER.

1423
01:23:24,066 --> 01:23:28,370
WOW, IT’S EXPO ’67.

1424
01:23:28,370 --> 01:23:30,105
ROWSDOWER.

1425
01:23:30,105 --> 01:23:34,343
A WHOLE NOTHER CITY
TO FAIL IN.

1426
01:23:34,343 --> 01:23:38,146
I WONDER IF THEY NEED
SNOW PLOWING SERVICES.

1427
01:23:38,146 --> 01:23:41,016
AUDREY HEPBURN--
OH, IT’S TROY.

1428
01:23:45,621 --> 01:23:49,291
WELL, SON OF A BUCK,
THAT JUST FLEW UP THERE.

1429
01:23:52,694 --> 01:23:56,632
LUKE, IT IS YOUR DESTINY.

1430
01:24:01,570 --> 01:24:02,704
HM?

1431
01:24:02,704 --> 01:24:06,575
SUSAN DEY!
OH, NO, IT’S TROY. SORRY.

1432
01:24:06,575 --> 01:24:08,944
HE’S GONNA TURN
INTO A WAR-WILF.

1433
01:24:08,944 --> 01:24:11,780
HOW ABOUT A SMOKE, KID?

1434
01:24:14,082 --> 01:24:16,518
HEY, THE NEOSPORIN
REALLY WORKED.

1435
01:24:16,518 --> 01:24:17,886
ALL RIGHT!

1436
01:24:17,886 --> 01:24:22,658
MY DRINKIN’ ARM’S HEALED!

1437
01:24:22,658 --> 01:24:24,860
UH, ROWSDOWER,
YOU’RE SQUEEZING MY--

1438
01:24:24,860 --> 01:24:27,529
ROW-- [CRACKING SOUNDS]
ROWSDOWER. ROW...

1439
01:24:28,797 --> 01:24:31,733
OOH, THAT SHOT
CONTAINS TOO MUCH NOSTRIL.

1440
01:24:33,969 --> 01:24:35,671
OH, HECK, I CAN’T BELIEVE
THE ANCIENT CITY

1441
01:24:35,671 --> 01:24:39,608
KICKED US OUT ALREADY.

1442
01:24:39,608 --> 01:24:42,244
JOIN US NEXT WEEK
WHEN TROY AND ZAP BATTLE

1443
01:24:42,244 --> 01:24:45,347
AN ARMY OF EVIL ACADIAN ROBOTS
ON CAPE BRETON.

1444
01:24:45,347 --> 01:24:47,149
THEN IN UPCOMING WEEKS,
THEY’LL TAKE ON

1445
01:24:47,149 --> 01:24:49,651
A BAND OF ZOMBIE FUR TRAPPERS
IN MEDICINE HAT.

1446
01:24:49,651 --> 01:24:53,221
THAT’S ON ZAP AND TROY,
THE LEGENDARY JOURNEYS.

1447
01:24:54,823 --> 01:24:57,960
[HUMMING]

1448
01:25:01,463 --> 01:25:05,367
♪ OH, BABY,
ROWSDOWER SAVES US ♪

1449
01:25:05,367 --> 01:25:08,837
♪ AND SAVES ALL THE WORLD ♪

1450
01:25:11,173 --> 01:25:14,609
♪ HE COMES TO SAVE THE DAY
IN A BROKEN TRUCK ♪

1451
01:25:14,609 --> 01:25:18,747
♪ WITH A STINKY DENIM JACKET
ON HIS BACK ♪

1452
01:25:18,747 --> 01:25:22,284
♪ HE COULDN’T HELP THIS MOVIE
WHICH REALLY SUCKED ♪

1453
01:25:22,284 --> 01:25:26,488
♪ BUT AT LEAST WE DIDN’T HAVE TO
SEE HIM PLAY HACKEYSACK ♪

1454
01:25:26,488 --> 01:25:27,823
WHAT?

1455
01:25:27,823 --> 01:25:28,924
I’M SORRY, I PANICKED.

1456
01:25:28,924 --> 01:25:30,726
WAKE UP. THIS IS
IMPORTANT TO ME DAMNIT.

1457
01:25:30,726 --> 01:25:32,427
WELL, I’LL TRY TO DO BETTER.

1458
01:25:32,427 --> 01:25:34,029
SSH, HERE IT COMES. LISTEN.

1459
01:25:34,029 --> 01:25:36,898
♪ ROWSDOWER SAVES US ♪

1460
01:25:36,898 --> 01:25:41,403
♪ AND SAVES ALL THE WORLD ♪

1461
01:25:41,403 --> 01:25:43,705
♪ ROWSDOWER SAVES-- ♪

1462
01:25:43,705 --> 01:25:44,906
NO, NO, NO, MIKE,
THAT SECTION’S OVER,

1463
01:25:44,906 --> 01:25:46,141
YOU NON-MUSICAL MOOK.

1464
01:25:46,141 --> 01:25:47,743
- WELL, SORRY.
- NEVER MIND.

1465
01:25:47,743 --> 01:25:49,177
I’LL HANDLE
THIS SECTION MYSELF.

1466
01:25:49,177 --> 01:25:51,179
TALK QUIETLY
AMONGST YOURSELVES.

1467
01:25:51,179 --> 01:25:52,914
♪ DANNY ELFMAN,
DANNY ELFMAN ♪

1468
01:25:52,914 --> 01:25:54,516
♪ THIS SONG SOUNDS
LIKE DANNY ELFMAN ♪

1469
01:25:54,516 --> 01:25:56,918
♪ IT JUST SOUNDS
LIKE DANNY ELFMAN
DANNY ELFMAN ♪

1470
01:25:56,918 --> 01:26:00,155
♪ HE’S THE DAD OF JENNA ELFMAN,
JENNA ELFMAN, JENNA ELFMAN ♪

1471
01:26:00,155 --> 01:26:01,590
♪ HE’S THE DAUGHTER
OF DANNY ELFMAN ♪

1472
01:26:01,590 --> 01:26:03,425
♪ DANNY ELFMAN,
DANNY ELFMAN ♪

1473
01:26:03,425 --> 01:26:05,260
SAY, MIKE, YOU KNOW,
I DIDN’T THINK THIS MOVIE

1474
01:26:05,260 --> 01:26:06,862
WAS AS BAD AS THE USUAL FARE.

1475
01:26:06,862 --> 01:26:08,530
YOU’RE JOKING I HOPE.

1476
01:26:08,530 --> 01:26:11,033
NO, NO, NO.
ADMITTEDLY IT HAD SOME FLAWS.

1477
01:26:11,033 --> 01:26:13,001
IT WAS A LITTLE OVERZEALOUS
PURSUING SOME OF ITS IDEAS,

1478
01:26:13,001 --> 01:26:16,038
GRANTED, BUT I THINK IT WAS
MORE OF A PROBLEM OF FORM.

1479
01:26:16,038 --> 01:26:17,606
A MOVIE IS JUST NOT
THE RIGHT MEDIUM

1480
01:26:17,606 --> 01:26:18,840
FOR THIS MATERIAL.

1481
01:26:18,840 --> 01:26:21,476
IT NEEDS TV.
IT NEEDS TO BE A SERIES.

1482
01:26:21,476 --> 01:26:23,278
HM, I DON’T KNOW.

1483
01:26:23,278 --> 01:26:24,880
JUST LET ME
PITCH THIS TO YOU.

1484
01:26:24,880 --> 01:26:26,782
UH, OKAY, I’M LISTENING. GO.

1485
01:26:26,782 --> 01:26:28,450
GREAT, GREAT,
THANKS FOR HEARING ME OUT.

1486
01:26:28,450 --> 01:26:30,819
 OKAY, THE FINAL SACRIFICE,
 THE SERIES.

1487
01:26:30,819 --> 01:26:32,654
- THE NAME GOES.
- WHAT?

1488
01:26:32,654 --> 01:26:35,323
NEVER LIKED THE NAME.
THE NAME GOES. IT’S BANAL.

1489
01:26:35,323 --> 01:26:37,759
BUT IF YOU’RE HOPING
TO CONNECT THE SERIES
WITH THE MOVIE, MIKE--

1490
01:26:37,759 --> 01:26:39,861
WE NEED SOMETHING LIKE,
OH, NIGHT MISTRESS.

1491
01:26:39,861 --> 01:26:41,229
NIGHT MISTRESS?

1492
01:26:41,229 --> 01:26:42,731
YEAH, OR CLOOTCHI
AND THE LIEUTENANT.

1493
01:26:42,731 --> 01:26:44,366
YOU KNOW, SOMETHING
THAT’S GOING TO SEDUCE PEOPLE.

1494
01:26:44,366 --> 01:26:46,201
REALLY CONNECT WITH THEM.
WE’LL WORK ON THAT.

1495
01:26:46,201 --> 01:26:47,969
OKAY. OKAY...

1496
01:26:47,969 --> 01:26:50,505
SO YOU GOT ROWSDOWER,
AND HE ROAMS THROUGH CANADA,

1497
01:26:50,505 --> 01:26:52,040
AND HE’S GOT
HIS LITTLE PAL TROY,

1498
01:26:52,040 --> 01:26:53,809
AND THEY ALL GET INTO
ALL KINDS OF SCRAPES.

1499
01:26:53,809 --> 01:26:55,444
- BUT THEY HELP PEOPLE--
- ALABAMA.

1500
01:26:55,444 --> 01:26:58,313
- WHAT?
- ALABAMA, CHICAGO, CLEVELAND.

1501
01:26:58,313 --> 01:27:00,315
NO, I LIKE ALABAMA.
YOU LIKE ALABAMA? 

1502
01:27:00,315 --> 01:27:01,616
IT’S YOUR SHOW.

1503
01:27:01,616 --> 01:27:03,118
WELL, TO ME,
CANADA IS THE ESSENCE--

1504
01:27:03,118 --> 01:27:05,020
PITTSBURGH, WE’LL DO IT
IN PITTSBURGH.

1505
01:27:05,020 --> 01:27:07,489
WELL, I SUPPOSE IF YOU ACTUALLY
FILM IT IN PITTSBURGH--

1506
01:27:07,489 --> 01:27:09,558
NO, NO, NO, WE FILM IN CANADA.
HAVE TO.

1507
01:27:09,558 --> 01:27:10,692
[BEEP]

1508
01:27:10,692 --> 01:27:13,428
HOLD ON. YEAH, JUDY.
OKAY, THANKS.

1509
01:27:13,428 --> 01:27:14,529
YOU GOT TWO MINUTES.

1510
01:27:14,529 --> 01:27:16,031
GUTTENBERG’S PEOPLE
ARE COMING IN.

1511
01:27:16,031 --> 01:27:18,133
WHAT DO YOU MEAN
GUTTENBERG’S PEOPLE
ARE COMING IN?

1512
01:27:18,133 --> 01:27:20,135
WHAT I MEAN IS
YOU JUST LOST A MINUTE. GO.

1513
01:27:20,135 --> 01:27:21,503
WHOA, SORRY, SORRY.

1514
01:27:21,503 --> 01:27:24,139
SO, THE LEAD CHARACTER
IS ROWSDOWER, OF COURSE.

1515
01:27:24,139 --> 01:27:26,241
LEAD CHARACTER’S THE KID,
SPARKY McHOOLIHAN

1516
01:27:26,241 --> 01:27:27,375
OR WHATEVER THE HELL
HIS NAME WAS.

1517
01:27:27,375 --> 01:27:28,910
YOU LIKE THAT NAME?
I NEVER LIKED THAT NAME.

1518
01:27:28,910 --> 01:27:30,512
WELL, THAT’S NOT HIS NAME.
I MEAN...

1519
01:27:30,512 --> 01:27:33,415
BUT I LIKE ALL THAT
FUNNY BEER STUFF YOU GET
WITH THAT ROWSDOWER GUY.

1520
01:27:33,415 --> 01:27:34,850
HIM BEING A HOPELESS DRUNK
AND ALL THAT.

1521
01:27:34,850 --> 01:27:37,352
HE’S LOVEABLE, YOU KNOW?
HE FALLS DOWN, HE’S SICK A LOT,

1522
01:27:37,352 --> 01:27:38,487
BUT HE’S LOVEABLE.

1523
01:27:38,487 --> 01:27:40,489
AND THE KID,
THE KID WORKS IN A BREWERY.

1524
01:27:40,489 --> 01:27:42,858
I ACTUALLY HAD
AN HOUR-LONG DRAMA IN MIND.

1525
01:27:42,858 --> 01:27:44,793
WHAT ARE YOU, ONE OF THOSE
DENNIS FRANZ FREAKS, HUH?

1526
01:27:44,793 --> 01:27:46,128
NOW, WAIT A MINUTE--

1527
01:27:46,128 --> 01:27:47,596
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT, YEAH,
GIVE ME A SECOND HERE.

1528
01:27:47,596 --> 01:27:48,930
I’M GOING SOMEWHERE.
I’M THERE, I’M THERE.

1529
01:27:48,930 --> 01:27:51,199
THIS ROWSDOWER GUY,
FULL FRONTAL, YOU KNOW?

1530
01:27:51,199 --> 01:27:52,567
COUPLE TIMES A SEASON.

1531
01:27:52,567 --> 01:27:54,402
TASTEFUL, LOW LIGHTS,
JUST A HINT.

1532
01:27:54,402 --> 01:27:56,471
[BEEP]
HOLD ON. YES, JUDY.

1533
01:27:56,471 --> 01:27:57,939
I KNOW. YOU GOT 30 SECONDS.

1534
01:27:57,939 --> 01:28:00,542
OKAY, WELL THIS MAIN CHARACTER,
UM, SPARKY--

1535
01:28:00,542 --> 01:28:01,977
HAS A FRIEND, A GIRL.

1536
01:28:01,977 --> 01:28:03,545
HELL, HE’S A GIRL TOO.
THERE ARE A LOT OF GIRLS.

1537
01:28:03,545 --> 01:28:04,713
THEY’RE ALL ROOMMATES.

1538
01:28:04,713 --> 01:28:06,081
THERE’S A GOOFY GIRL,
A SERIOUS GIRL,

1539
01:28:06,081 --> 01:28:07,482
A CHEERLEADER,
THE LOOSE GIRL.

1540
01:28:07,482 --> 01:28:09,451
EVERYBODY IN THE DAMN SERIES
IS A DAMN GIRL!

1541
01:28:09,451 --> 01:28:11,753
- YEAH, BUT ROWSDOWER--
- A BIG, HAIRY GIRL!

1542
01:28:11,753 --> 01:28:13,054
[BEEP]
YES, JUDY. I’LL TELL YOU WHAT.

1543
01:28:13,054 --> 01:28:14,689
I GOT A SHOW IDEA FOR YOU.

1544
01:28:14,689 --> 01:28:16,725
YOU GET OUT OF MY OFFICE
UNTIL YOU GIVE ME SOMETHING
I CAN USE.

1545
01:28:16,725 --> 01:28:18,527
-NOW I GOTTA GO MEET
GUTENBERG’S PEOPLE.
- WHOA!

1546
01:28:18,527 --> 01:28:20,128
GEE WHIZ.

1547
01:28:20,128 --> 01:28:22,197
[HUMMING CONTINUES]

1548
01:28:25,534 --> 01:28:27,135
HEY, WHERE’S THE MUSIC?

1549
01:28:27,135 --> 01:28:29,804
YOU GUYS!

1550
01:28:29,804 --> 01:28:31,673
THE END!

1551
01:28:43,051 --> 01:28:45,220
WE SHALL MEET AT MIDNIGHT,
AND THEN--

1552
01:28:45,220 --> 01:28:47,622
- HELLO, MIKE.
- HI, FELLAS. HOW’S IT GOING?

1553
01:28:47,622 --> 01:28:49,824
- NICE FLOWERS.
- THANKS.

1554
01:28:49,824 --> 01:28:53,461
HEY! YOU GUYS DIDN’T TAKE AND GO
AND START A CULT, DID YOU?

1555
01:28:53,461 --> 01:28:54,729
[COUGHS] 
A CULT?

1556
01:28:54,729 --> 01:28:56,598
A CULT? NO, OF COURSE NOT.

1557
01:28:56,598 --> 01:28:59,401
THAT IS THE MOST ABSURD THING--
WELL, YEAH WE DID.

1558
01:28:59,401 --> 01:29:00,468
YEAH, YOU WANT TO JOIN?

1559
01:29:00,468 --> 01:29:01,803
NO, I DON’T WANT TO JOIN.

1560
01:29:01,803 --> 01:29:03,939
YOU’LL PROBABLY BE SACRIFICING
BLACK PULLETS,

1561
01:29:03,939 --> 01:29:05,240
AND WEARING GOAT HEADS
AND THINGS.

1562
01:29:05,240 --> 01:29:06,341
WELL, YOU KNOW,
WE THOUGHT ABOUT ALL THAT,

1563
01:29:06,341 --> 01:29:07,976
BUT IT JUST SEEMED
LIKE A LOT OF WORK.

1564
01:29:07,976 --> 01:29:09,411
ACTUALLY WE JUST
LIKE TO BAKE MUFFINS.

1565
01:29:09,411 --> 01:29:10,779
LOTS OF DIFFERENT KINDS.

1566
01:29:10,779 --> 01:29:11,947
YEAH, THEN WE GET TOGETHER
AT EACH OTHER’S HOUSES,

1567
01:29:11,947 --> 01:29:13,415
AND WATCH ALLY McBEAL.

1568
01:29:13,415 --> 01:29:15,717
OR ONE OF OUR COLLECTION
OF TAPED  SISTERS  EPISODES.

1569
01:29:15,717 --> 01:29:17,385
YEAH, WE’RE KIND OF
A MUFFINEY,

1570
01:29:17,385 --> 01:29:19,821
CALISTA FLOCKHEART,
SWOOSIE KURTZ KIND OF CULT.

1571
01:29:19,821 --> 01:29:21,556
YEAH.

1572
01:29:21,556 --> 01:29:22,824
UM, MIKE?

1573
01:29:22,824 --> 01:29:24,626
OH, BOY.
I THINK WE FREAKED HIM OUT.

1574
01:29:24,626 --> 01:29:26,294
WHOA. OKAY, MIKE.

1575
01:29:26,294 --> 01:29:28,863
WE STRIP TO THE WAIST,
WORSHIP AN EVIL EMANATION,

1576
01:29:28,863 --> 01:29:30,865
AND LOP PEOPLE’S HEADS OFF
FOR FUN.

1577
01:29:30,865 --> 01:29:31,967
IS THAT LESS WEIRD?

1578
01:29:31,967 --> 01:29:33,568
AH, YEAH, THAT’S
A LITTLE EASIER TO TAKE.

1579
01:29:33,568 --> 01:29:35,303
- GOOD.
- OH, UH, PEARL’S CALLING.

1580
01:29:35,303 --> 01:29:36,338
[GROWLING]

1581
01:29:36,338 --> 01:29:38,340
AH, NELSON.

1582
01:29:38,340 --> 01:29:40,575
SO GLAD WE COULD JOIN YOU.

1583
01:29:40,575 --> 01:29:43,645
FOR, YOU SEE, I AM ABOUT TO TAKE
A GIANT STEP FORWARD

1584
01:29:43,645 --> 01:29:45,580
IN MY PROGRAM
TO TAKE OVER THE WORLD,

1585
01:29:45,580 --> 01:29:47,649
ONE PERSON AT A TIME.

1586
01:29:47,649 --> 01:29:49,918
AFTER HOURS
OF TOUGH NEGOTIATION,

1587
01:29:49,918 --> 01:29:52,354
I AM ABOUT TO POSSESS
THE MIND,

1588
01:29:52,354 --> 01:29:54,489
THE SOUL, THE VERY WILL

1589
01:29:54,489 --> 01:29:56,958
OF THIS MAN HERE.

1590
01:29:56,958 --> 01:29:58,426
WHAT WAS YOUR NAME AGAIN?

1591
01:29:58,426 --> 01:29:59,661
CARL.

1592
01:29:59,661 --> 01:30:00,895
ALL RIGHT, CARL.

1593
01:30:00,895 --> 01:30:02,764
YOU’VE COWERED
AT MY THREATS,

1594
01:30:02,764 --> 01:30:04,900
YOU’VE RELISHED MY REWARDS,

1595
01:30:04,900 --> 01:30:06,601
YOU’VE EATEN ME OUT
OF HOUSE AND HOME,

1596
01:30:06,601 --> 01:30:07,969
NOW SIGN.

1597
01:30:07,969 --> 01:30:09,271
CERTAINLY, MY LIEGE.

1598
01:30:09,271 --> 01:30:14,009
 [PHONE RINGING]
 HANG ON. LET ME GET THIS.

1599
01:30:14,009 --> 01:30:16,511
YEAH. REALLY?

1600
01:30:16,511 --> 01:30:18,046
HOW MUCH?

1601
01:30:18,046 --> 01:30:19,748
SOUNDS GOOD. THANKS.

1602
01:30:19,748 --> 01:30:20,949
I’M SORRY, LADY.

1603
01:30:20,949 --> 01:30:22,484
I WAS JUST TAKEN OVER
BY THE TRAVELERS GROUP.

1604
01:30:22,484 --> 01:30:23,652
GOTTA RUN. BYE.

1605
01:30:23,652 --> 01:30:26,855
- MONKEY, WHITEY...
- WE’RE ON IT.

1606
01:30:26,855 --> 01:30:31,559
I GUESS THE MRS. MR. NICE GUY
APPROACH JUST AIN’T MY STYLE.

1607
01:30:31,559 --> 01:30:34,562
[CACKLES]

1608
01:30:34,562 --> 01:30:38,933
SO VERY SHORTLY NOW, NELSON,
I WILL RULE CARL!

1609
01:30:38,933 --> 01:30:41,703
UNTIE ME OR YOU’LL HAVE TO
ANSWER TO THE TRAVELERS GROUP!

1610
01:30:41,703 --> 01:30:43,071
GIVE ME BACK MY FOOD!

1611
01:30:43,071 --> 01:30:45,607
NO! UGH!

1612
01:30:45,607 --> 01:30:47,542
♪♪

1613
01:31:49,104 --> 01:31:51,906
ROWSDOWER.
